1	https://academicprograms.usc.edu/services/undergraduate-research-and-experiential-learning/usc-provosts-undergraduate-research-fellowships/	2026-11-13 18:44:54.714245-08	200	USC Provost’s Undergraduate Research Fellowships - Office of Academic Programs Skip to main content Go to usc.edu homepage Office of Academic Programs Home Services Show submenu for Services Academic Advising Academic Integrity Curriculum Excellence in Teaching Student Success Undergraduate Research and Experiential Learning Offices and Units Show submenu for Offices and Units Academic Exploration Advising Academic Honors and Fellowships Center for Excellence in Teaching Graduate School Kortschak Center for Learning and Creativity Norman Topping Student Aid Fund Office of Academic Integrity USC President’s High Tech Scholars About More… Show More Menu Search for: Home » Services » Undergraduate Research and Experiential Learning » USC Provost’s Undergraduate Research Fellowships USC Provost’s Undergraduate Research Fellowships Grant Period: Spring 2027 (Note: Should COVID-19 rates increase, we ask all faculty supervisors and their students to conduct their research projects remotely) The Office of the Provost will provide a limited number of fellowships for undergraduate research each academic year in the fall, spring, and summer terms. Each undergraduate student funded by the program will receive a stipend in the amount of $1000 ($3000 in the Summer) to support research in any academic field for a period of not less than ten weeks at 8-10 hours per week for Fall and Spring, and 20 hours per week in the Summer (no less than eight weeks) during the awarded term. All full-time USC faculty actively engaged in research are eligible to serve as faculty supervisors. Application Instructions Applications will be available beginning Tuesday, October 20, 2026. Eligible undergraduate students will submit the following information by Tuesday, November 19, 2026 (11:59 pm) deadline to be considered for funding: Please select the “ Submit Application ” option (also listed below). You will also be asked to include your intended research project (one page 500-word limit) on the application. Students should use the text box provided on the portal (preferred). If you have images (i.e., symbols, charts, graphs, etc.,) you may want to use the browser feature on the application to upload your one-page project description. Provost Faculty Supervisor Recommendation. The SMA portal will generate an email to faculty supervisors so that they can complete an online form or upload a faculty recommendation letter through a link provided to them via their USC email address. Please note: Faculty Supervisor Recommendation Forms are valid for one year. Faculty whose previous recommendation forms are less than a year old are encouraged to enter “Use faculty recommendation already on file” when submitting their recommendation form through the portal. Faculty may either upload their recommendation letters using the upload browser feature or copy and paste their recommendation in the text box provided through the portal. Each faculty mentor may nominate only one candidate for the USC Provost Fellowship Program, ensuring focused support and equitable consideration across departments . All funding decisions will be announced by mid-January 2027. Please note : If you find an error in your application, please contact Dr. Glasgow via email at dglasgow@usc.edu so that he can move it back into draft mode. Ensure that you select the SUBMIT option to officially submit your application . All applications that are in draft mode will not be considered for funding. Do NOT create and submit multiple applications . Lastly, use your USC email address when submitting your application. Submit Application Student Eligibility Requirements Enrollment of 12 or more units at USC during Spring 2027 in a program leading to an undergraduate degree (Progressive Degree students are ineligible to apply for Provost Fellowship awards). Prior volunteer or funded research experience with a research active USC faculty member is preferred. USC cumulative GPA of 3.0 or better. Preference will be given to students whose USC cumulative GPA is 3.5 or better. Students must complete at least 64 units (includes Transfer and AP) before submitting a Provost Fellowship application. Current Provost Fellowship recipients who plan to apply for a fellowship for the upcoming semester or term must submit an online application, an updated project description, a faculty recommendation letter (valid for one year only), and a two-page final summary report (due at the end of the semester). Students will be notified by Dr. Glasgow via email of their two-page summary report a few weeks before the next cycle application deadline for guidelines (see FAQs titled “What is a two-page report and what should I include in it?). All students who received a Provost Fellowship this semester and intend to reapply for the upcoming semester/term must complete another online Provost Fellowship application (to include an updated project description and final summary report) for the upcoming semester/term. All funding decisions will be announced around mid-January 2027. Direct Deposit Stipend Instructions If you are a US citizen or permanent resident, you may receive your stipend by direct deposit to a checking or savings account. To opt into direct deposit, you can set up an account by inputting the information online in Workday using this guide . If you are an international student, you will receive the stipend via your USC e-Pay account. Please update your local and permanent addresses in ExperienceUSC . If you are awarded a fellowship and do not have Direct Deposit, your stipend checks will be mailed to your local address directly from USC Financial & Business Services. Checks are normally sent to students during the third week of the month (as requested by your faculty supervisor). Please ensure your local address is accurate on ExperienceUSC at the beginning of each semester/term. We cannot pick them up from the University Payroll Office and distribute them to students from our office. IF YOU ALREADY HAVE DIRECT DEPOSIT, it is not necessary to resubmit the form. All funding decisions will be announced by mid-January. Please note: If you find an error in your application, please contact dglasgow@usc.edu to request your application to be placed into draft status. Please be sure to select the SUBMIT option when you have made your changes to the application. Frequently Asked Questions If you have any questions, please read the FAQ. Otherwise, contact us below. For students inquiring about the status of their payments, please contact aphelp@usc.edu and inform them that you have not received your payment. Read FAQs Contact If you have any questions, please contact Dr. David Glasgow via email at dglasgow@usc.edu . Site Navigation Academic Programs Services Offices and Units About Services Curriculum Academic Advising Academic Integrity Student Success Undergraduate Research and Experiential Learning Excellence in Teaching Offices and Units Graduate School Academic Exploration Advising Academic Honors and Fellowships Norman Topping Student Aid Fund Kortschak Center for Learning and Creativity Office of Academic Integrity Center for Excellence in Teaching USC President’s High Tech Scholars Quick Links Graduate Admissions Website myGradSchool Portal Transfer Student Soul Search University of Southern California Content managed by the Office of Academic Programs Office of Academic Programs University of Southern California 3601 Trousdale Parkway, Student Union 301 Los Angeles, CA 90089-0894 (213) 740-9033 academic.programs@usc.edu Built using the USC Gateway 2018 WordPress Theme | Website issues? Contact USC Provost IT Privacy Notice | Notice of Non-discrimination | Digital Accessibility | Sitemap Translate	a483296a44ea59bb43b0a4d409ce66913fffda4c73fc85fcac204f427be10bd6	\N
2	https://annenberg.usc.edu/current-students/resources/annenberg-scholarships-and-awards	2026-11-13 18:44:54.714245-08	200	Annenberg Scholarships and Awards | USC Annenberg School for Communication and Journalism -->Skip to main content Menu Close Search Close What are you looking for? Academics Undergraduate Majors Master's Programs PhD Program Minors Professional and Executive Programs Admissions Graduate Applicants Undergraduate Applicants Connect and Visit Tuition and Financial Aid About School Leadership Mission and Vision Commencement Contact Us Faculty Faculty and Staff Resources Student Experience Advisement and Academic Services International Programs Career Development Progressive Degrees Organizations USC Annenberg’s Media Center Student Work Research Alumni News Events Giving Open Search Form Open Mobile Navigation Academics Undergraduate Majors Master's Programs PhD Program Minors Professional and Executive Programs Admissions Graduate Applicants Undergraduate Applicants Connect and Visit Tuition and Financial Aid About School Leadership Mission and Vision Commencement Contact Us Faculty Faculty and Staff Resources Student Experience Advisement and Academic Services International Programs Career Development Progressive Degrees Organizations USC Annenberg’s Media Center Student Work Research Alumni News Events Giving Current Students » Resources Annenberg Scholarships and Awards Thanks to the support of generous donors, USC Annenberg offers a diverse array of student aid.* Applicants must be currently enrolled in a USC Annenberg major or degree program to be eligible for an award. Some awards are available year-round, while others are awarded annually. For those awards given annually, please check back early during the Spring semester to access the application. *Students who are immediate or extended family members, dependents or other relatives of the donor(s) or selection committee members are not eligible to receive scholarships from these funds. Student aid available year-round Student Emergency Aid Fund Eligibility criteria: Undergraduate or graduate All undergraduate majors and graduate degree programs Must demonstrate financial need Awards vary based upon each student’s unique circumstances Average award: $1,000 Awards are distributed to students experiencing unforeseen circumstances and emergencies impacting their ability to pay tuition or cover everyday living expenses. These awards are not intended to cover full-tuition expenses, but rather serve as bridge funding to guarantee students’ continued enrollment at USC until other resources, such as scholarships or loans, become available. Students are encouraged to provide as much information in their application, as well as contact their academic adviser directly with questions about additional resources available to them. Apply to the Student Emergency Aid Fund Student Success Fund Eligibility criteria: Undergraduate or graduate All undergraduate majors and graduate degree programs Must demonstrate financial need Awards vary based upon each student’s unique circumstances Average award: $1,000 Awards will be distributed throughout the year via an application process to students pursuing extra- and co-curricular programs and opportunities not covered by tuition. Funding is available for, but not limited to: participation in experiential-learning programs offered by USC Annenberg, including Maymester expenses related to internships, such as travel and lodging non-tuition costs arising from study abroad registration, travel and lodging costs incurred for professional and career development conferences, seminars and workshops, and expenses related to student research and assignments, such as capstone projects, which might require additional travel and lodging costs beyond what is covered by tuition Apply to the Student Success Fund In the case of the Student Emergency Aid Fund and the Student Success Fund, please be aware that: Funding is not guaranteed. Awards will be given on a first-come, first-served basis. Due to the high volume of requests, students will only be notified if funds become available. Awards are given in the form of a one-time stipend. The Financial Aid Office is notified of all stipends. Stipends qualify as part of a student’s financial aid package. Therefore, a stipend might reduce other financial aid that you have been awarded, depending on the type of aid received. It is the student’s responsibility to contact the Financial Aid Office with any questions regarding your financial aid package. Kaleigh Finnie Memorial Endowment Fund Eligibility criteria: Undergraduate or graduate All undergraduate majors and graduate degree programs Awards available up to $3,000. Established in memory of USC Annenberg student Kaleigh Finnie, this fund supports students whose work seeks to address the ongoing mental health crisis. This merit-based fund provides scholarships and awards to USC Annenberg undergraduate or graduate students who will leverage communication, journalism and/or public relations to contribute critical research and generate important conversations around mental health. Applicants will be asked to provide a description of their research interest or project relating to mental health. Applications will open on August 24 and are due Monday, September 18, 2026 at 12 p.m. Apply to the Kaleigh Finnie Memorial Endowment Fund Center for Health Journalism's Domestic Violence Student Impact Reporting Fund Eligibility criteria: Undergraduate (junior or senior) or graduate students in journalism Awards available between $500–$3,000. This fund provides student journalists with a roadmap for reporting about domestic violence with nuance and sensitivity. By participating in this program, students will have an opportunity to gain valuable insights, while receiving mentoring, project editing and a grant to support their work. Applications are due Friday, October 3, 2025. Apply to the Domestic Violence Student Impact Reporting Fund Undergraduate Journalism Scholarships When Undergraduate Journalism Scholarships become available, they will be listed here. Undergraduate Public Relations Awards When Undergraduate Public Relations Awards become available, they will be listed here. Undergraduate and Graduate Journalism Scholarships Allan Malamud Scholarship Eligibility criteria: Undergraduate or Graduate, Journalism, Need-based, Merit-based Positive consideration will be given to students who are of Junior or Senior class standing and who demonstrate an interest in sports journalism. Award: 4 awards of $6,500 (2 grad and 2 UG students) The application deadline is May 20, 2026 Apply to the Allan Malamud Scholarship youtube twitter linkedin instagram flickr facebook COVID-19 Information Annenberg Media Annenberg Digital Lounge Faculty and Staff Resources Brightspace Privacy Policy myUSC Emergency Information Notice of Nondiscrimination USC Annenberg School for Communication and Journalism | 3502 Watt Way | Los Angeles, California 90089-0281 © 2026 University of Southern California. All Rights Reserved.	add67fd4c34c8dbc84c5bc8938b64e7269213910640cbe0fa115cfb26e2d5dbd	\N
3	https://awardsdatabase.usc.edu/app/detail.asp?FellowshipID=283	2026-11-13 18:44:54.714245-08	200	USC Awards and Fellowships Database University of Southern California Awards and Fellowships Database Office of the Provost Menu Skip to content Skip to secondary content Undergraduate Honors & Fellowships USC Graduate School Find an Opportunity Share an Opportunity Return to Content Breadcrumb Navigation Awards and Fellowships Database Find an Opportunity Find an Opportunity Back USC Viterbi Scholarships for Continuing Students Description Each year, continuing undergraduates should be re-evaluating their need and merit-based aid opportunities. This page helps to outline current available funding sources for continuing undergraduate students at the USC Viterbi School of Engineering. In most cases the primary resource for financial assistance is need-based aid provided by the USC Financial Aid Office. Please visit their website for information on applying for and receiving aid as well as a listing of several scholarship resources. Be sure to pay special attention to all of their deadlines! In addition to applying for need-based aid, continuing undergraduate students within the Viterbi School can apply for various donor-supported scholarships each year via the Viterbi Scholarship Application. Any continuing undergraduate student who has received the Viterbi School Merit Scholarship and/or the Merit Research Award must also submit the application for renewal every year by the deadline. Eligiblity Information Academic Level: Undergraduate Age minimum or maximum:* No Open to international students: Yes Required to demonstrate financial need: No Discipline Area(s): Engineering Minimum GPA: Yes If yes, what is the minimum? 3.0 Demographic Information (preferred or required) : USC students Award type: Scholarship Amount Awarded: Amount varies Application Information: Application Deadline: March Date application is available: USC endorsement required: No Contact Information: Website: http://viterbiundergrad.usc.edu/finaid/ Awards and Fellowships Database Find an Opportunity Share an Opportunity - Partner Portal Undergraduate Honors & Fellowships Student Union, 300 (213) 740-9116 ahfstaff@usc.edu USC Graduate School Student Union, 301 (213) 740-9033 gradsch@usc.edu Feedback Content managed by USC Academic Honors & Fellowships Database Designed by IVC Productions, LLC	b40b787f86131b0276ebeaae73f37062104353ac67d4d2c792d8820760e8e68e	\N
4	https://campussupport.usc.edu/	2026-11-13 18:44:54.714245-08	200	Campus Support and Intervention - Campus Support & Intervention Skip to main content Go to usc.edu homepage Campus Support & Intervention Home About Us Students Show submenu for Students First-Time Consultation Academics Health & Wellness Show submenu for Health & Wellness Health Leave Basic Needs Crisis & Safety Emergency Loan Application Faculty & Staff Show submenu for Faculty & Staff Report a Concern Resources Families, Parents & Guardians TC4T Health Leave Show submenu for Health Leave Resources & Forms Frequently Asked Questions More… Show More Menu Search for: Campus Support and Intervention Support for USC The Office of Campus Support & Intervention (CSI) is where members of the Trojan community go to seek support for themselves, for others, and for the community. We are a one-stop shop for care and support, troubleshooting, and advocacy. If you would like to connect with a CSI team member, please call at 213-740-0411 or email at uscsupport@usc.edu . A member of our team will respond to emails within one business day. Health Leave of Absence for Students For more information about the Health Leave process, including how to schedule an online appointment, please visit our Health Leave page. Who We Are Campus Support & Intervention (CSI) is an office within Campus Wellbeing and Crisis Intervention. Our team is here to assist current students, faculty, and staff in navigating complex issues. Whether you are here seeking support for yourself or someone else, we are available to help you problem solve, understand options, and connect with resources. Please note that we are not an emergency resource and are not available 24/7. In case of an emergency, please contact the Department of Public Safety at 213-740-4321. What We Do Students, faculty, and staff may encounter challenges that disrupt their ability to succeed and meet their goals. CSI is dedicated to helping individuals get back on track by providing options and pathways for success. We connect with members of the USC community when they need support in achieving their academic, professional, or personal goals. Our consultations, available in person, via Zoom, or over the phone, allow us to understand each individual’s situation so we can offer troubleshooting, support, guidance, and connections to relevant campus and community resources. Below are some of the ways CSI serves the USC community: Navigation of complex issues and challenges Resource referrals and recommendations Critical incident response and postvention support Solutions and options Trojans Care 4 Trojans (TC4T) – A reporting program for concerns about someone’s well-being Professor notifications* DPS incident follow-up Student Health Leave of Absence Crisis as you define it *Notifications are made on a case-by-case basis when a student is unable to make the notifications on their own behalf. Please consult with a staff member regarding these requests. Students Need support, but don’t know where to start? Discover the resources available to you and schedule to speak directly with a team member. Faculty & Staff Are you a faculty or staff member seeking support? Explore the resources available to you. If you’re concerned about a student, CSI can collaborate with you to provide outreach and assistance. Families, Parents & Guardians Worried about your student? Learn about some of the resources available to them and how you can partner with CSI to support them through any challenges they may be facing. Trojans Care 4 Trojans (TC4T) USC Trojans Care for Trojans (TC4T) is an initiative within the Office of Campus Wellbeing and Crisis Intervention that empowers USC students, faculty and staff to take action when they are concerned about a fellow Trojan challenged with personal difficulties. This private and anonymous request form provides an opportunity for Trojans to help a member of our Trojan Family. Submit a concern Campus Support & Intervention Tutor Campus Center, TCC Suite 421 Los Angeles, CA 90089 (213) 740-0411 uscsupport@usc.edu Related Sites Campus Wellbeing & Crisis Intervention Campus Wellbeing & Education USC Office of the Ombuds Concerned about a USC community member? TC4T is a private and anonymous form to help a member of the Trojan Family. Submit a concern University Links University Human Resources Office for Equity, Equal Opportunity, and Title IX Office of Professionalism and Ethics Office of Culture, Ethics, and Compliance How to Report a Concern – USC Report & Response University of Southern California Built using the USC Gateway 2018 WordPress Theme | Website issues? Contact USC Provost IT Privacy Notice | Notice of Non-discrimination | Digital Accessibility | Sitemap Translate	602938ded5dbd33888140797112ae034228d92d208316211c095e6ccee9d8c95	\N
5	https://campussupport.usc.edu/students/basic-needs/emergency-loan-application/	2026-11-13 18:44:54.714245-08	200	Emergency Loan Application - Campus Support & Intervention Skip to main content Go to usc.edu homepage Campus Support & Intervention Home About Us Students Show submenu for Students First-Time Consultation Academics Health & Wellness Show submenu for Health & Wellness Health Leave Basic Needs Crisis & Safety Emergency Loan Application Faculty & Staff Show submenu for Faculty & Staff Report a Concern Resources Families, Parents & Guardians TC4T Health Leave Show submenu for Health Leave Resources & Forms Frequently Asked Questions More… Show More Menu Search for: Emergency Loan Application For students struggling with severe financial hardship *UPDATE: Emergency Loan Applications – Fall 2026 The Emergency Loan Application is currently closed for the Fall 2026 semester. Students seeking additional support are encouraged to review available resources or contact our office with questions about other resources that may be appropriate. The Campus Support & Intervention (CSI) Emergency Loan program is available for students who have experienced an unforeseen financial emergency. Students may receive one loan per/semester not exceeding $1,000. Students are highly encouraged to consult with the Financial Aid Office and their respective academic unit prior to applying for an emergency loan. Eligibility Currently enrolled Good financial standing with USC – does not have a negative balance in collections U.S.A. issued Social Security Number Must demonstrate need by providing documentation verifying the emergency Must demonstrate the financial capacity to fulfill repayment obligations What is an Emergency? Family emergency, loss of employment, natural disasters, medical emergencies and other unexpected issues that suddenly change your financial circumstances Policy Details CSI may approve loans of up to $1000 per student. Please allow five to ten business days for processing. Emergency loans must be repaid through Student Financial Services within 90 days. If an emergency loan is not repaid within 90 days, a 10% annual interest rate will be applied, the account will be sent to collections, and a registration hold will be placed. Failure to repay will also result in students becoming ineligible for future emergency loans. CSI reserves the right to decline any application, regardless of eligibility. Emergency Loan Application Form Please fill out the form below and someone from Campus Support & Intervention will contact you within one to two business days. Full Name (Required) First Last Student ID (Required) Do you have a Social Security Number? (Required) A SSN is required for the loan application. Upon approval, a staff member will contact you via phone to obtain it. Yes No Current Address (Required) Street Address City Alabama Alaska American Samoa Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Guam Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Northern Mariana Islands Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Puerto Rico Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah U.S. Virgin Islands Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Armed Forces Americas Armed Forces Europe Armed Forces Pacific State ZIP Code Cell Phone (Required) Email Address Are you currently enrolled as a student at USC? Yes No Are you currently employed in a paying position? Yes No Are you currently receiving financial aid? Yes No Describe your efforts to obtain assistance through other sources. (Financial Aid appeal, academic unit, family, friends, organizations, etc.) Describe how you will be able to repay the emergency loan within 90 days. Describe your financial situation in your own words. Include what expenses the emergency fund would be used for and attach appropriate documentation to this application. Please share with us anything you feel is relevant. Please upload supporting documentation explaining your financial situation. While it is not required in order to submit your Emergency Loan application, supporting documentation will allow us to review your request more quickly and accurately. If you choose not to include supporting documentation, it might be requested after your application is submitted, which could delay the review process further. Drop files here or Select files Max. file size: 15 MB. Emergency loan amount you are requesting Please enter a number less than or equal to 1000 . CAPTCHA Email This field is for validation purposes and should be left unchanged. Campus Support & Intervention Tutor Campus Center, TCC Suite 421 Los Angeles, CA 90089 (213) 740-0411 uscsupport@usc.edu Related Sites Campus Wellbeing & Crisis Intervention Campus Wellbeing & Education USC Office of the Ombuds Concerned about a USC community member? TC4T is a private and anonymous form to help a member of the Trojan Family. Submit a concern University Links University Human Resources Office for Equity, Equal Opportunity, and Title IX Office of Professionalism and Ethics Office of Culture, Ethics, and Compliance How to Report a Concern – USC Report & Response University of Southern California Built using the USC Gateway 2018 WordPress Theme | Website issues? Contact USC Provost IT Privacy Notice | Notice of Non-discrimination | Digital Accessibility | Sitemap Translate	e45c99de830e7044d81ad2f76c2a6a356c6dcae0d9c1acde0a690b502fc9bae3	\N
6	https://careers.usc.edu/channels/appointments/	2026-11-13 18:44:54.714245-08	200	Appointments – Career Center | University of Southern California Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Career Center Schedule An Appointment Handshake Who We Serve Audiences Incoming Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Ph.D.’s & Postdoctoral Students Employers Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Affinities First-Generation Students International Students Student Accessibility Veteran Students Our Services Appointments Workshops & Trojan Talks Career Fairs & Events Professional Headshots Scholarships Trojan Network Make A Request Online Resources Get Career Ready Career Exploration Career Readiness Competencies Explore Industries Resumes/Cover Letters/Curriculum Vitaes Mentors & Networking Interview Preparation Offer Negotiation Financial Literacy Education and Events AI Guidelines Find Internships & Jobs On-Campus Jobs Campus Recruiting Handshake Internship Guide Job Search Guide Trojan Network Trojan Accountability Expectations Connect With Us About Us Get Involved Meet the Team Meet Our Partners School-Based Career Services Report a Fraudulent Job Posting Career Outcomes First Destination Survey Summer Experience Survey Appointments Find information on making appointments and requests below. 24/7 Support Looking for Resume Assistance NOW? Career Center Resume Guide Quinncia is USC’s new AI career prep platform available to current students starting Fall 2026 Generative AI Guidelines for resume prompts when using Generative AI Want Interviewing Support NOW? The USC Career Center is proud to provide all students and alumni with Big Interview – an interactive platform that provides 24/7 access to interview practice opportunities, customized feedback, etc. Current students can also access Quinncia for additional mock interviewing prep based on your resume upload. Interested in a career assessment NOW? The Your Next Step platform provides various career assessments and helps clarify career goals. This resource offers you access to career opportunities, prepares you for interviews, and assists you in executing a strategic job search. Interested in specialized resources? Many school-based career centers have curated resources and services specifically for the students in their majors. Please consider making an appointment with a career advisor from your school-based career center. Drop-in Advising Drop-in advising is designed to help students connect with a career advisor to ask basic career questions, explore career resources, or get a quick critique of your resume or cover letter. Fall & Spring: Drop-in advising is available in-person in STU 110 from 1:00-3:30 pm Summer: 15-minute resume review critiques are available via appointment on Handshake Many school-based career centers provide school-specific advising as well. For resume and cover letter support, we encourage you to use the following resources: Resume Resources on Handshake to view the USC Career Center online resource library on Handshake Cover Letter, Resume, and CV guide with samples to review Resume workshops featured on the USC Career Center YouTube channel Details: Each drop-in session is 10-15 minutes. Drop-ins are available on a first-come, first-served basis. During peak times, students may be asked to participate in group drop-in advising sessions to ensure timely support for everyone. An active Handshake account is required to check-in for all drop-ins. Log in to Handshake and complete your student profile to activate your account. Students are limited to one advising contact per day (appointment or drop-in advising). Scheduled Appointments Career Advisors provide 30-minute appointments via phone, Zoom or in-person. Many school-based career centers have career advisors to schedule appointments with as well. During scheduled 30-minute appointments, USC Career Center advisors typically advise on the following topics: Career Development Internship and Job Search Informational Interviews & Networking Offer/Salary Negotiation Mock Interviews Note: If you want the Career Advisors to tailor interview questions for you, please email the advisor you are scheduled with and provide your resume and a copy of a job description at least two business days in advance after your appointment request is confirmed. Please note: Resume critiques are only conducted during drop-in advising (1:00 pm – 3:30 pm Monday through Friday, no appointment needed) To schedule a 30-minute appointment: Log in to Handshake . Go to Career Center, then click on Appointments. Click “ Schedule a New Appointment ” and choose USC Career Center – Current Students. Search for available appointments that meet your needs. You will have the opportunity to select either a virtual or in-person appointment. If you opt for a virtual session please be specific in the appointment request notes and be sure to indicate whether you prefer to have your appointment via phone or video chat (Zoom). Video appointment: the advisor will email you a Zoom link to your USC email address once the appointment is approved. Learn how to create your Zoom account . Phone appointment: please include your phone number in your appointment request. In-person appointments: Will be held in USC Career Center lobby (Student Union, Suite 110, University Park Campus). Undergraduate Students Our policy is one appointment (drop-in or 30-minute) per day, so please plan accordingly. Graduate Students Are limited to one advising appointment with the central Career Center before being referred to your college for more industry-specific advising. Graduate students are encouraged to attend Career Center workshops, fairs, and other events and utilize online resources available in Handshake. Non-degree Students Please be advised that career advising appointments and drop-ins are for current students in certificate and degree programs. Pre-master’s students may request appointments upon enrollment in Master’s coursework. If you have any questions please email careers@usc.edu Students Responsibility in Scheduling Career Appointments Once your scheduled career advising appointment is approved, please ensure you attend your meeting or cancel within 48 hours or two business days prior to your appointment. If you need to cancel your career advising appointment, please email careers@usc.edu or call 213 740-9111 and leave a message. If you fail to cancel within 48 hours, your career advising privileges may be revoked. Alumni (0-3 years following graduation) Please refer to the Alumni Career page for advising information. Additional questions can be directed to careers@usc.edu Mock Interview Appointments Scheduled a mock interview? If you want us to tailor mock interview questions, please email your career advisor at least two full business days before your appointment with: A detailed job description of interest A recent copy of your resume Please review Interview Preparation for additional tips. If you do not send us a job description, the advisor will ask you general interview questions. We highly encourage you to practice interviewing BEFORE your mock interview using Big Interview or Quinncia . This 24/7 resource allows you to select interview questions, record and review your answers. Online Resources The USC Career Center offers multiple resources to help individuals explore their career opportunities. We have curated several of our favorite resources to help discover career paths, learn about internship positions, and find full-time jobs. Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link Handshake Updated June 19, 2026 Handshake is USC’s university-wide career services management platform and the largest career community for college students. … Read More School-Based Career Services Share This: Share School-Based Career Services on Facebook Share School-Based Career Services on LinkedIn Share School-Based Career Services on X Copy Link Career Services at the University of Southern California Along with the USC Career Center , USC has school-based career services offices … Read More Back to top ↑ View More Online Resources Make a Request We are here to help you in any way we can. Please select from the following: Request a Career Center Speaker Share This: Share Request a Career Center Speaker on Facebook Share Request a Career Center Speaker on LinkedIn Share Request a Career Center Speaker on X Copy Link Our mission is to enhance career development through partnerships and innovative technology in preparation for global career aspirations. To that … Request a Speaker Request an Accessibility Accommodation for Career Center Appointments or Events Share This: Share Request an Accessibility Accommodation for Career Center Appointments or Events on Facebook Share Request an Accessibility Accommodation for Career Center Appointments or Events on LinkedIn Share Request an Accessibility Accommodation for Career Center Appointments or Events on X Copy Link The USC Career Center welcomes all of our community’s different cultures, identities, talents, and interests. We strive to be consistently … Read More Back to top ↑ View More Forms News | Events | Jobs and Internships | Experiential Learning Opportunities | Mentors | Resources | Videos Student Union 110 Los Angeles, CA 90089-4897 (213) 740-9111 (213) 740-9104 USC Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Make an Appointment Contact Us Office Hours Monday - Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Social Media LinkedIn Instagram YouTube About Us Learn About the Career Center USC Facts & Figures Who Recruits at USC? Meet Our Partners Join Our Team Digital Accessibility Notice of Non-Discrimination The USC Career Center operates all of its programs and activities consistent with the University's Notice of Non-Discrimination . Eligibility is not determined based on race, sex, ethnicity, sexual orientation, or any other proh