 Institute Bridge Institute Center for Computational Language Sciences Center for Ecological and Evolutionary Dynamics Center for Music, Brain and Society Center for New Technologies in Drug Discovery and Development Center for Peptide and Protein Engineering Center for the Changing Family Center for Synthetic Living Systems Convergent Science Institute in Cancer Dana and David Dornsife Cognitive Neuroimaging Center New Microbes For New Beneficial Natural Products Psychology Services Center USC Sea Grant PHYSICAL SCIENCES Agilent Center of Excellence in Biomolecular Characterization Center for Applied Mathematical Sciences Center for Quantum Information and Science Technology Center of Excellence in Molecular Characterization Center of Excellence in NanoBiophysics Core Center of Excellence in Nano Imaging Loker Hydrocarbon Research Institute Statewide California Earthquake Center The Plastics Problem The Urban Critical Zone Explore All Browse all of our departments, programs, centers, and institutes Continuing Student Scholarships MENU Home Dornsife Continuing Student Scholarships Application Scholarship Descriptions Recommendations FAQ Research, Travel, and Internship Grants Other Scholarships Continuing Student Scholarship application The USC Dornsife Continuing Student Scholarship application is a single application used to apply for a range of scholarships offered to continuing undergraduate students with a major in USC Dornsife. Scholarships range in amount from $1,000 to $6,000 per year. The total number of scholarships awarded varies. The application opens every spring semester and awards are applied towards the following academic year. Award notifications are sent in June. To be eligible to apply you must: Have a declared USC Dornsife major Be enrolled full-time as an undergraduate student (12 units or more) Have a minimum cumulative USC GPA of 3.0 Spring admits with no USC GPA may apply, but must meet the application’s GPA requirement by the end of the spring semester if selected for an award. During the awarded academic year, scholarship recipients must: Maintain a USC Dornsife major Be enrolled full-time as an undergraduate student during both fall and spring semesters (12 units or more) Maintain a minimum cumulative USC GPA of 3.0 Students graduating in the fall semester of the awarded year are eligible to apply. These are awards for continuing students only. Students graduating before the start of the academic year to which the award applies are not eligible for consideration. Scholarships through this application process are one-time awards. You must reapply each year to continue receiving a scholarship award. Receiving (or not receiving) a scholarship a previous year has no bearing on whether or not you will receive a scholarship for the upcoming year. To view a current list of scholarships available through the Dornsife Continuing Student Scholarship application process, visit the Scholarship Descriptions page . The 2026-2027 Dornsife Continuing Student Scholarship application deadline has passed. The 2027-2028 Dornsife Continuing Student Scholarship application will be available in January 2027. Other Scholarships: A handful of scholarships for continuing undergraduate students do not utilize the USC Dornsife Continuing Student Scholarship application. These scholarships each have their own unique scholarship criteria, applications, and application deadlines. Visit the Other Scholarship Applications page for more information on these additional scholarship opportunities for continuing undergraduate USC Dornsife students. Important dates: The application deadline for the 2026-2027 USC Dornsife Continuing Student Scholarships has passed. Please visit this webpage in January 2027 for information for the 2027-2028 USC Dornsife Continuing Student Scholarships application. Contact Details Contact us If you have additional questions, please contact our office. We’re happy to help! USC Dornsife Admission and Student S