er 2027). The funding is credited to the student’s university account. This may affect student financial aid packages. It is the student’s responsibility to contact the USC Financial Aid office ( askUSC ) to discuss the potential impact of an ExL award. All funds will be disbursed in accordance with University policies and procedures. Eligibility Requirements Declared major in Dornsife College of Letters, Arts and Sciences 3.0 cumulative USC GPA or better – Newly admitted students (freshmen, spring admits, or transfer) are not eligible to apply until a USC GPA is calculated. Full-time enrollment at USC for the Fall 2026 – Spring 2027 academic year (i.e., registered for 12 undergraduate units each semester). Seniors graduating in December 2026 and students who have completed 144 total units or more by the start of Fall 2026 are not eligible to apply Demonstrated financial need Dornsife-approved program, experience, etc., taking place between August 24 and December 1 (Fall 2026). Activity must not be part of course requirements or be receiving course credits. Students should contact financial aid for assistance with costs associated with a course. Must not have already received the maximum ExL funding during the academic year for which you are applying. Up to $1,500 can be awarded per academic year (Fall 2026-Summer 2027) Students who are receiving funding through SOAR, SURF, Provost Fellowship (PURF), other USC research, internship, or travel funding sources, funds from research lab or internship, or work-study positions will not be contemporaneously considered for ExL. Application Periods Fall 2026: Thursday, August 13, 2026 – Thursday, September 3, 2026 Spring 2027: Thursday, December 3, 2026 – Thursday, January 14, 2027 Summer 2027: Thursday, March 4, 2027- Thursday, April 8, 2027 Applications received after the priority application deadline will be reviewed on a first-come, first-served basis, as funding may not be available for those applying after the priority deadline. Please reach out via email if applying after the priority application deadline. All students, including previous ExL recipients, must submit a new application each funding cycle. Applications typically open at 4:00 PM PST and close at 5:00 PM PST. Need Assistance? If you experience any issues accessing the application, please contact us at soar@dornsife.usc.edu Application Components: To be considered for the ExL Award , applicants must submit all required materials as outlined below. Please ensure all documents are compiled and uploaded as a single PDF file for items 2-4 . 1. ExL Award Online Application Access the ExL Award application here . 2. Supporting Documents Include documentation verifying your participation in the experiential learning opportunity. Acceptable materials may include: Website of activity or event Event Itinerary Presentation Materials if presenting in a conference Conference registration or email confirmation Any official document confirming your participation in the experiential opportunity, including key details such as dates, location, and contact information 3. One-Page Personal Statement Provide a personal statement (maximum one page) responding to the following prompt: Tell us about yourself and how this experiential learning opportunity will enrich your studies and future goals. Share your achievements, experiences at USC, and interests, and tell us what you hope to gain from this experience. Additionally, indicate whether you have applied for any other grants or fellowships to support this opportunity. 4. Detailed Cost Sheet Submit a detailed breakdown of all eligible expenses related to your experiential learning opportunity. Examples of allowable costs include: Transportation or flight expenses Conference or program registration fees Lodging costs Your cost sheet should clearly outline itemized expenses and include an estimated total that supports the amount of funding you are requesting. Required Report At the conclusion of the experiential learning opportunity, ExL award recipients are required to submit a one-page report . The report is a brief summary of your overall experience. If you fail to submit the report, your ExL award funding will be rescinded and you will become ineligible for ExL award funding in future terms. The ExL award report should be submitted via the instructions indicated on the award agreement. Click here to access the ExL award report guidelines. ExL Report Deadlines: Fall 2026: Monday, December 21, 2026 Spring 2027: Monday, April 19, 2027 Summer 2027: Monday, August 2, 2027 Frequently Asked Questions Can I apply for multiple funding opportunities at USC? Yes, students are allowed to apply for multiple funding opportunities during the same period. However, you may only accept funding from one source for the same period. Also, students awarded the maximum amount of ExL award funding in the fall are not eligible to apply for additional funds in the spring or summer. You must disclose your intent to apply for other funding sources in your ExL application proposal. If you are offered and accept funding from another source before receiving notification from ExL, you are required to inform our office immediately. Your application for ExL will automatically be closed if you accept funds from another source. Any offers from ExL are also voided if you accept funds from other sources. Students who fail to disclose receiving multiple awards for their research or experiential learning opportunity will have their ExL award rescinded, and will become ineligible for SOAR/SURF/ExL funding in future terms. Q: Can the ExL award be used for course expenses, registration, or travel? No. EXL Awards are limited and intended to support experiential learning opportunities, service-learning activities, or conferences. Student’s receiving course credit are not eligible to apply. Students participating in eligible Maymester or Julymester programs should instead apply for SOAR funding. Students participating in an eligible Summer PWP course should apply for SURF funding. Q: How can I request that my funding be directly deposited into my bank account? Fall/Spring Award Recipients: You can receive your SOAR award by direct deposit to a checking or savings account. Please note that if you have outstanding tuition, fees, or other items on your student account, the SOAR award will go toward paying those first. If your fee bill has been fully paid, you may access the award as a refund. To receive a refund, log in to USCe.pay and sign up for direct deposit (under My Account). Summer Award Recipients: Please visit Direct Deposit Stipend Instructions for guidance. It is highly recommended that you sign up for direct deposit to avoid lost checks. Be advised that your stipend may arrive as a check mailed to your local home address. Students should always keep all addresses (both current address and permanent address) updated in OASIS. Contact Us USC Dornsife Admission and Student Success 3607 Trousdale Parkway, MHP 106, Los Angeles, CA 90089 soar@dornsife.usc.edu Academics Majors and Minors Undergraduate Education Master’s & Professional Studies PhD Studies Scholarship Award Non-Discrimination Directories & Maps Our Faculty Our Staff Social Media Directory Campus Maps Access & Support Dornsife Technology Services Brand and Identity MyDornsife 365 Web USC Zoom Trojan Family Alumni Relations USC Dornsife Magazine Dornsife Dialogues Commencement Career Pathways Dornsife at a Glance Contact Us Privacy Digital Accessibility Emergency Information Notice of Non-Discrimination Copyright © 2026 University of Southern California	f0f0be73ec5fb46c14030ebeadaafc1cafe4d6885c8d0cdd0549412c7176025b	\N
