ENCES Brain and Creativity Institute Bridge Institute Center for Computational Language Sciences Center for Ecological and Evolutionary Dynamics Center for Music, Brain and Society Center for New Technologies in Drug Discovery and Development Center for Peptide and Protein Engineering Center for the Changing Family Center for Synthetic Living Systems Convergent Science Institute in Cancer Dana and David Dornsife Cognitive Neuroimaging Center New Microbes For New Beneficial Natural Products Psychology Services Center USC Sea Grant PHYSICAL SCIENCES Agilent Center of Excellence in Biomolecular Characterization Center for Applied Mathematical Sciences Center for Quantum Information and Science Technology Center of Excellence in Molecular Characterization Center of Excellence in NanoBiophysics Core Center of Excellence in Nano Imaging Loker Hydrocarbon Research Institute Statewide California Earthquake Center The Plastics Problem The Urban Critical Zone Explore All Browse all of our departments, programs, centers, and institutes Continuing Student Scholarships MENU Home Dornsife Continuing Student Scholarships Application Scholarship Descriptions Recommendations FAQ Research, Travel, and Internship Grants Other Scholarships Dornsife Research, Travel, and Internship Grant Programs Hands-on learning outside the classroom can expand your horizons and enrich your education in countless ways. USC Dornsife is proud to support students engaging in academic research, overseas study, internships, and other experiential learning opportunities. Click on the boxes to learn more about our various types of awards. Undergraduate Grants Student Opportunities for Academic Research (SOAR) Dornsife students engaging in faculty-led research during the fall and/or spring semesters are encouraged to apply for up to $1,000 in funding through the SOAR program. This includes spring Maymesters and fall Julymesters that involve a research component. Summer Undergraduate Research Fund (SURF) / Summer Humanities Undergraduate Research Fund (SHURE) SURF and SHURE provide up to $3,000 in funding for Dornsife students participating in faculty-led research during the summer. Students participating in Problems without Passports (PWP) summer courses are also eligible to apply. Major-Specific Research and Internship Grants Students pursuing research and internship opportunities, in selected majors, whether on or off campus, may be eligible to apply for an award to support these hands-on learning experiences. Major-Specific Travel Grants Students pursuing overseas study in selected majors or to selected countries may be eligible to apply for an award to support these hands-on learning opportunities. ExL Award The ExL Award supports Dornsife undergraduates interested in participating in hands-on learning opportunities such as service learning, professional conferences, or overseas study. Students must have a minimum GPA of 3.0 and a declared Dornsife major. Gateway Internship Pay It Forward Scholarship By gaining real world experience through an internship, students add to their academic pursuits and strengthen career skills. The Pay It Forward Scholarship is awarded to sophomores, juniors, and seniors at USC Dornsife who participate in an unpaid summer internship at a non-profit 501 (c) organization or government agency. Center for Advanced Genocide Research Fellowships The USC Dornsife Center for Advanced Genocide Research offers fellowships for students from any academic discipline to conduct original research drawing on the unique resources in Holocaust and Genocide Studies at USC including the Holocaust and Genocide Studies book collection, the Special Collections at USC Libraries, and the Visual History Archive. Other Travel Scholarships The USC Office of Overseas Studies has collected information on a number of scholarship opportunities, both within and outside USC, to support study abroad. Other Internship Grants The USC Career Pathways office has collected information on a number of funding sources for participation in internships. Contact Details Contact us If you have further questions, please contact our office. We’re happy to help! USC Dornsife Admission and Student Success (213) 740-5930 scholarships@dornsife.usc.edu Academics Majors and Minors Undergraduate Education Master’s & Professional Studies PhD Studies Scholarship Award Non-Discrimination Directories & Maps Our Faculty Our Staff Social Media Directory Campus Maps Access & Support Dornsife Technology Services Brand and Identity MyDornsife 365 Web USC Zoom Trojan Family Alumni Relations USC Dornsife Magazine Dornsife Dialogues Commencement Career Pathways Dornsife at a Glance Contact Us Privacy Digital Accessibility Emergency Information Notice of Non-Discrimination Copyright © 2026 University of Southern California	b403afb4238b1f0fc5bd5267e24c0daab9bf2b5b5c7393eba017ef6849046b35	\N
