d Faculty PSI Instructors PSI Blog Contact Us Research News Research Newsletters About About Sol Price and the Naming Gift About the Dean Board of Councilors Dean’s Cabinet Annual Report Core Values USC Price Among Best Public Affairs Schools Fight On in Los Angeles Moving Forward: Community Dialogue and Engagement Listen Learn Meet the Team Giving to Price International Alumni Ways to Give Endowment Gifts Contact the Dean’s Office Career Services Alumni Careers Career Services and Student Resources Career Education and Programming Internships and Fellowships David Bohnett Leadership Fellowship at the L.A. County Board of Supervisors Price Scholars for Community Enrichment Internship Fund International Students Internship Documentation Fall Networking Night Alumni Resources and Programs Employer Resources USC Price Virtual Recruitment and Engagement Fair USC Career Center Employment Data BSPP 2024 Employment Data BSUSP 2024 Employment Data MNLM 2024 Employment Data MHA 2024 Employment Data MPA 2024 Employment Data MPP 2024 Employment Data MUP 2024 Employment Data Contact Us Current Students News All News Events Supporting Price Info Sessions Request Info Apply Menu Open Search University of Southern California Search Site Funding Your Education Graduate Scholarships and Financial Aid Our graduate scholarships are open to domestic, international, and undocumented students unless noted otherwise. All scholarships offered through the USC Sol Price School of Public Policy are administered consistent with the University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination. Recipients are chosen without regard to race, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, or any other prohibited characteristic. Subscribe to our scholarship newsletter here to be notified of USC and outside scholarship opportunities each month! How to Apply Many scholarships are awarded as part of the admissions process or have deadlines that coincide with admission application deadlines. For this reason, students should begin researching scholarship opportunities early, as many deadlines occur before admission decisions are released. While some scholarships are automatically considered through the admissions process, others require a separate application through Scholarship Universe or directly with the scholarship provider. To maximize your opportunities, complete these three steps: Apply to USC Some scholarships will be granted based on information in your admission application. Merit-based scholarships will be automatically granted to those who qualify and apply by required deadlines. Learn More About Scholarships Apply for Financial Aid Some scholarships may consider your financial need as part of the selection process. Submitting your FAFSA or CADAA will help ensure you can apply to all types of scholarships. Apply for Financial Aid Apply at Scholarship Universe Scholarship Universe is a scholarship matching tool that identifies relevant scholarships based on your personalized profile. Scholarship Universe Graduate Scholarship Opportunities Find Your Scholarships Title Open To Amount Application Opens Deadline How to Apply City Hall Fellows Scholarship Program Details Scholarships for students who have completed the San Francisco City Hall Fellows program. Awards are disbursed $5,000 the first year and $5,000 the second year. Scholarship is automatically renewable assuming satisfactory academic progress. Incoming students Up to $10,000 8/1/2026 12/15/2026 To apply, please complete the Dean’s Merit Scholarship Application which is part of the USC Graduate Application for Admission. Apply Now City/County Management Fellowship Program Scholarships Details Scholarships based on academic merit awarded to students who express an interest in a career in local government. City/County Management Fellows are mentored by and participate in meetings and programs hosted by the City/County Management Board, a group of influential city and county managers. In addition, the Board provides stipends for conference travel. Awards are renewal for the second year assuming satisfactory academic progress. Incoming students 25% to full tuition 8/1/2026 12/15/2026 To apply, please complete the CMF Scholarship application which is part of the USC Graduate Application for Admission. Apply Now David C. Bohnett Endowed Leadership Fund Details The David C. Bohnett Leadership Fund provides masters-level public policy students with valuable hands-on experience in local government through a one-year fellowship with the Los Angeles County Board of Supervisors. Fellows assist the Chair (office) of the Board of Supervisors as liaison between constituents, other governmental agencies, non-profits and other stakeholders and the board offices. The Price Office of Career Services manages this fellowship’s recruitment process. Applicants will learn of the opportunity in mid-September and will apply by mid-October. Continuing students Full tuition (second year) and $29,000 stipend 10/8/2026 10/30/2026 The application is available in Handshake. Students must log in using the “Student Log-In” option. Handshake Dean’s Merit Scholarship (Online Programs) Details Submit a 300-word essay directly through the online application that answers the following questions: Why are you considering completing your graduate studies at USC’s Sol Price School of Public Policy? Which USC Price faculty are you interested in working with, and why? What do you consider USC Price’s most unique features to be? The scholarship renews until degree completion as long as the student maintains at least a 3.0 cumulative GPA and maintains satisfactory academic progress. Incoming students Varies Ongoing June 15, October 1, January 15 Submit a 300-word essay directly through the online application. Apply Now Dean’s Merit Scholarships (On-Campus Programs) Details The Dean’s Merit Scholarship is a tuition-only scholarship based on a holistic evaluation of candidates’ academic achievements, professional experiences, impact in their field, and alignment with the Price School’s mission. The scholarship is open to domestic, undocumented, and international students admitted into the fall semester for the following on-campus programs: Master of Public Administration, Master of Public Policy, Master of Health Administration, or Master of Urban Planning. Incoming students 25% to full tuition 8/1/2026 12/15/2026 To apply, please complete the Dean’s Merit Scholarship Application which is part of the USC Graduate Application for Admission. Apply Now Dollinger Master of Real Estate Development Scholarships Details Each year, the Dollinger MRED program awards a limited number of partial tuition scholarships to entering full-time MRED students. Scholarships are awarded as part of the admission process. Funding sources within the Dollinger MRED program include: Bornstein Endowed Scholarship Ko Chieh Chi MRED Scholarship First American Endowed Scholarships Greenlaw Partners Endowed Scholarship George and Shirley Isaacs Endowed Scholarship Alan Kreditor Endowed Scholarship Lusk Center for Real Estate Scholarships Incoming students $10,000 – $50,000 to 16 units of tuition credit 8/1/2026 2/1/2027 To be considered, applicants must submit all application materials along with the USC Price Dean’s Merit Scholarship application (found online with the USC Graduate Application under the Supplemental Forms section) by February 1. Apply Now James Irvine California Scholarships Incoming students Varies August 4, 2026 December 15, 2026 Submit your graduate application for fall admission to an eligible program by December 15. To be considered for additional funding, respond to supplemental scholarship questions found within the Program Materials section of the graduate admission application. Apply Now Price Scholars for Community Enrichment Endowment Fund Incoming students Up to full tuition & $5,500 stipend August 4, 2026 December 15, 2026 The application is available in Scholarship Universe. Prospective students log in using their youSC credentials. Continuing students log in using their USC Net ID and password. Application Portal Red and Sheri Cavaney Endowed Scholarship for Nonprofit Leadership Details A scholarship for a student in the Master of Nonprofit Leadership and Management degree. Special consideration will be given to a student whose career interest is in working in a trade or professional association. Incoming students, Continuing students Up to $4,000 December 1, 2026 March 21, 2027 The application is available in Scholarship Universe. Prospective students are automatically considered during the admissions process. Continuing students must apply through Scholarship Universe and login using their USC Net ID and password. Scholarship Universe Red and Sheri Cavaney Graduate Veteran Scholarship Details A scholarship for a Price master’s degree student who is a veteran of the US Military. Preference will be given to an individual with academic and career goals that include an interest in using their policy background to examine opportunities for economic growth and job creation. Incoming students, Continuing students Up to $5,000 December 1, 2026 March 21, 2027 The application is available in Scholarship Universe. Prospective students are automatically considered during the admissions process. Continuing students must apply through Scholarship Universe and login using their USC Net ID and password. Scholarship Universe Scholarships for Domestic Applicants Outside of California Details The University of Southern California Sol Price School of Public Policy announces the establishment of scholarships for domestic applicants outside of California. The Price School is committed to providing access to higher education for domestic, non-California residents. Incoming students Varies August 4, 2026 December 15, 2026 Submit your graduate application for fall admission to an eligible program by December 15. To be considered for additional funding, respond to supplemental scholarship questions found within the Program Materials section of the graduate admission application Apply Now Sutter Fellowship in Health Administration Details Scholarships for graduate students enrolled in the on-campus Master of Health Administration program at the University Park Campus. Scholarships aim to recognize leadership experience or potential for leadership and a commitment to making a positive impact to underrepresented communities in health-related fields Incoming students, Continuing students Up to $3,000 December 1, 2026 March 21, 2027 The application is available in Scholarship Universe. Prospective students are automatically considered during the admissions process. Continuing students must apply through Scholarship Universe and login using their USC Net ID and password. Scholarship Universe USC Asian Pacific Alumni Association Scholarships Details The USC Asian Pacific Alumni Association awards scholarships to USC students of exceptional academic merit. Positive consideration may be given in the selection process to students to promote diversity and/or to students who advocate for Asian and Pacific Islander communities. Incoming students, Continuing students Varies Expected December 2026 Expected March 2027 Asian Pacific Alumni Association USC Black Alumni Association Scholarships Details BAA scholarships are based upon the overall profile of a student’s commitment and aspirations gleaned from their application and interview. Scholarships are awarded to USC students on the basis of academic and personal merit in addition to having demonstrated involvement within the African-American community. Incoming students, Continuing students Up to $3,000 Expected December 2026 Expected February 2027 Black Alumni Association USC Lambda LGBTQ+ Association Scholarship Details Since 1994, USC Lambda has awarded over $500,000 in scholarships to more than 150 students who, regardless of their gender or sexual identity, demonstrated academic achievement and a strong commitment to the LGBTQ+ community. These scholars have gone on to executive roles in Fortune 500 companies and LGBTQ+ nonprofits. They have spearheaded research in technology and sociology, produced award-winning films, and argued cases before the United States Supreme Court. They are doctors, educators, artists and activists who inspire our LGBTQ+ student body to see their sexual and gender identities as strengths, not obstacles. Incoming students, Continuing students Varies Expected December 2026 Expected February 2027 Lambda LGBTQ+ Alumni Association USC Latino Alumni Association Scholarships Details LAA provides partial-tuition scholarships to USC undergraduate and graduate students who promote and/or advocate for the Latino/Hispanic community. Graduate scholarships are for master’s candidates only; limited awards for EdD, law, medical, PA, PT, OT, and doctor, of pharmacy students are also available. Incoming students, Continuing students $2,000 to $5,000 for undergraduate students; $500 to $5,000 for graduate students. Expected December 2026 Expected May 2027 Latino Alumni Association USC Norman Topping Student Aid Fund Undergraduate Scholarship Details The Norman Topping Student Aid Fund (NTSAF) assists students with financial need who demonstrate an extraordinary level of community awareness in their pursuit of higher education at the University of Southern California. Applicants residing in areas surrounding the University Park Campus and Health Sciences campus and first-generation college students are given primary consideration in the selection process. Please note that the scholarship is not limited to these populations. Incoming students Up to $5,500 undergraduates December 15, 2026 February 4, 2027 Norman Topping Student Aid Fund USC Price Visionary Scholarship Details The USC Sol Price School of Public Policy is proud to offer the Price Visionary Scholarships, intended to provide financial support to individuals who have demonstrated exceptional leadership and real-world impact in public service through full-time work, part-time roles, volunteerism, or a combination of the three. Visionary Scholars aspire to make an impact in professional fields such as public administration, public policy, health administration, urban planning, real estate development and related areas. These scholarships aim to empower students as they pursue one of the master’s degree programs offered at the USC Price School at the University Park Campus in Los Angeles. The scholarships welcome applicants at various stages of their careers—whether they bring several years of professional experience or have made an impact through volunteer work or other community involvement early in their journey. Recipients will be selected based on their demonstrated contributions to their field and their vision for building upon those achievements after completing their graduate education. Incoming students $10,000 TBD TBD Apply on Scholarship Universe Apply Now USC Price/City Year National Service Scholarships Details Scholarships for students who have served their communities through City Year. As a USC Price-City Year National Service Scholar, all admitted City Year AmeriCorps members, alumni, or staff will be awarded a scholarship in the amount equal to $5,000 of tuition, renewable for a second year ($10,000 over two years). Applicants qualify for an admission application fee waiver and will also be considered for additional merit-based aid based on the strength of the application. For application fee waiver, please visit the Office of Graduate Admission website . Incoming students Up to $10,000 8/1/2026 12/15/2026 To apply, please complete the Dean’s Merit Scholarship application which is part of the USC Graduate Application for Admission. Apply Now USC Price/COLFUTURO (Colombia) Fellowships Details A joint program between USC Price and Colombia’s COLFUTURO for graduate study at the Price School of Public Policy. The scholarship supports students from Colombia who will enroll in one of the USC Price two-year master’s degree programs (MHA, MPA, MUP, MPP, MNLM). Awards are disbursed $10,000 in the first year and $10,000 in the second year, assuming satisfactory academic progress. Incoming students Up to $20,000 8/1/2026 12/15/2026 To apply, please complete the Dean’s Merit Scholarship Application which is part of the USC Graduate Application for Admission. Apply Now USC Price/Coro Alumni Fellowships Details Up to $10,000 scholarship for students who have completed the Coro Public Affairs Fellows program. Awards are disbursed $5,000 in the first year and $5,000 in the second year of graduate study, assuming satisfactory academic progress. Incoming students Up to $10,000 8/1/2026 12/15/2026 To apply, please complete the Dean’s Merit Scholarship Application which is part of the USC Graduate Application for Admission. Apply Now USC Price/Fulbright Foreign Student Program Scholarship Details Merit-based scholarships for international students who are participating in the Fulbright Foreign Student Program to study at a U.S. institution. Fulbright Scholars who apply to admission by the December 15th deadline and are admitted are guaranteed a 50% tuition-only scholarship. Fulbright Scholars are expected to maintain full time enrollment, and the scholarship can renew for a second year assuming eligibility requirements are met. Incoming students 50% tuition 8/1/2026 12/15/2026 To apply, please complete the Dean’s Merit Scholarship application which is part of the USC Graduate Application for Admission. Apply Now USC Price/Peace Corps Paul D. Coverdell Fellowships Details USC Price is proud to offer the Peace Corps Paul D. Coverdell Fellowship for eligible Returned Peace Corps Volunteers (RCPVs). The Fellowship is a 25% tuition-only scholarship, renewable for a second year assuming eligibility requirements are met. Students may be eligible to receive additional Dean’s Merit Scholarship funding based on the strength of their application. Fellows are expected to secure and complete an internship that benefits an underserved community. For application fee waiver, please visit the Office of Graduate Admission website . Incoming students 25% tuition 8/1/2026 12/15/2026 To apply, please complete the Dean’s Merit Scholarship application which is part of the USC Graduate Application for Admission. Apply Now USC Price/Public Policy and International Affairs (PPIA) Scholarships Details Scholarships for students who have completed the Public Policy and International Affairs (PPIA) Summer Institute. Awards are disbursed up to $5,000 in the first year and $5,000 in the second year of graduate study, assuming satisfactory academic progress. For application fee waiver, please visit the Office of Graduate Admission website . Incoming students Up to $10,000 8/1/2026 12/15/2026 To apply, please complete the Dean’s Merit Scholarship application which is part of the USC Graduate Application for Admission. Apply Now USC Price/Republic of Korea Ministry of Personnel Management 1+1 Program Details USC Price will provide advanced graduate training for a select group of Republic of Korea employees. Applicants with outstanding academic credentials, strong English skills, recommendations, and financial support from the Korean government may qualify for a scholarship from USC Price. Awards are disbursed $12,00 in the first year and $12,000 in the second year, assuming satisfactory academic progress. Korean government officials will complete an internship along with their studies. All Korean government officials receiving the 1+1 long-term fellowship will be automatically considered. Incoming students Up to $24,000 8/1/2026 12/15/2026 To apply, please complete the USC Graduate Application for Admission by the January 15th deadline. Apply Now USC Price/Republic of Korea National Assembly Long-Term Fellowship Program Scholarships Details USC Price will provide advanced graduate training for a select group of Republic of Korea employees. Applicants with outstanding academic credentials, strong English skills, recommendations, and financial support from the Korean government may qualify for a scholarship from USC Price. Awards are disbursed $12,00 in the first year and $12,000 in the second year, assuming satisfactory academic progress. All Korean Government Officials receiving the Republic of Korea National Assembly Long-Term Fellowship will be automatically considered. Students pursuing the two year program complete an internship; students pursuing the MPA dual degree with Seoul National University do not compete an internship. Incoming students Up to $24,000 8/1/2026 1/15/2027 To apply, please complete the USC Graduate Application for Admission by the January 15th deadline. Apply Now USC Price/Teach for America Fellowships Details Up to $10,000 scholarship for students who are Teach for America alumni. Awards are disbursed $5,000 in the first year and $5,000 in the second year of graduate study, assuming satisfactory academic progress. For application fee waiver, please visit the Office of Graduate Admission website. Incoming students Up to $10,000 8/1/2026 12/15/2026 To apply, please complete the Dean’s Merit Scholarship application which is part of the USC Graduate Application for Admission. Apply Now USC Price/Veteran Administration Yellow Ribbon Matching Award Details USC Price is proud to partner with the U.S.Veterans Administration in providing matching VA Yellow Ribbon benefits to qualified students. The Price School has allocated funds for 23 Yellow Ribbon Awards each year at up to $5,000 for each award. The Yellow Ribbon Program provides additional funding for veterans who wish to attend private institutions. Funds can be used to meet any or all unmet tuition/fee needs, but cannot exceed the total cost of tuition and fees. Incoming students, Continuing students Up to $5,000 August 1, 2025 July 31, 2026 For award consideration, students must be admitted into a USC degree seeking program, enroll in classes, and certify for their veteran education benefits with the USC Veteran’s Certification Office. Per federal regulations, eligible recipients will be selected on a first-come/first-served basis. The USC Veterans Certification Office will then notify the Price School of Yellow Ribbon eligibility to request a matching award on behalf of the student. USC Veteran’s Certification Office USC Staff Assembly Scholarship Details The USC Staff Assembly Scholarship Program recognizes USC staff members who best represent the USC staff community while simultaneously dedicating themselves to academic excellence by earning a degree at USC. The program grants six awards of $1000 and the Lincoln Riley Staff Scholarship of $5000. Incoming students, Continuing students $1,000 – $5,000 Expected March 2027 Expected May 2027 USC Staff Assembly Scholarship Program USC Town and Gown Scholarships Details Available to U.S. citizens or permanent residents of Southern California with a minimum unweighted GPA of 3.4. Additional considerations include school activities, community engagement, leadership roles and accolades. An interview is required. Incoming students, Continuing students Undergraduates $10,000 per year; Graduate students $15,000 per year July 1, 2026 November 15, 2026 Town and Gown of USC In this section: Request Admission Information Info Sessions & Events Visit USC Price Schedule a Campus Tour Visit Preparation Application Deadlines Funding Your Education Undergraduate Scholarships and Financial Aid Graduate Scholarships and Financial Aid Price Community Enrichment Scholarship Scholarships Spotlight Price Partnerships Talk to a Price Ambassador Mentorship for an Accessible Price (MAP) Meet the MAP Board Price Student Ambassador Program (PSA) On-Campus Master’s Degree Program FAQ Graduate School Fair Schedule Contact USC Price Admission Staff USC Price Ralph and Goldy Lewis Hall 312 Los Angeles, California 90089-0626 (213)