ility Scholarships USC Air Force ROTC Interest Forms Departments A Hub for Addressing Urban Issues Urban Challenges Urban News Policy Impact and Community Engagement Learning in Los Angeles Admission & Aid Request Admission Information Info Sessions & Events Visit USC Price Schedule a Campus Tour Visit Preparation Application Deadlines Funding Your Education Undergraduate Scholarships and Financial Aid Graduate Scholarships and Financial Aid Price Community Enrichment Scholarship Scholarships Spotlight Price Partnerships Talk to a Price Ambassador Mentorship for an Accessible Price (MAP) Meet the MAP Board Price Student Ambassador Program (PSA) On-Campus Master’s Degree Program FAQ Graduate School Fair Schedule Contact USC Price Admission Staff Faculty Faculty Directory Price Kudos Research Centers and Initiatives Research Areas Economic Development Environment Governance Housing Security Nonprofit Management Public Policy and Administration Real Estate Security and Risk Analysis Social Innovation Transportation Urban Planning Health Policy and Management Bedrosian Center on Governance and the Public Enterprise About Watch Listen Events Fellows Symposium Contact Us Democracy and Governance Workshop Center for Health Financing, Policy and Management Center for Inclusive Democracy Center on Philanthropy and Public Policy Center for Risk and Economic Analysis of Threats and Emergencies (CREATE) Lusk Center for Real Estate METRANS Transportation Center PIPE Collaborative About the PIPE Collaborative Population Dynamics Research Group Safe Communities Institute (SCI) Schaeffer Center for Health Policy and Economics USC Schwarzenegger Institute for State and Global Policy Spatial Analysis Lab (SLAB) The Hispanic Well-Being Initiative Postdoctoral Fellows Urban Data Lab USC Center for Economic Development (CED) Center for Sustainability Solutions Center on National Defense and Public Safety (CNDPS) Public Safety Initiatives Courses and Programs PSI Videos PSI Spotlight USC Affiliated Faculty PSI Instructors PSI Blog Contact Us Research News Research Newsletters About About Sol Price and the Naming Gift About the Dean Board of Councilors Dean’s Cabinet Annual Report Core Values USC Price Among Best Public Affairs Schools Fight On in Los Angeles Moving Forward: Community Dialogue and Engagement Listen Learn Meet the Team Giving to Price International Alumni Ways to Give Endowment Gifts Contact the Dean’s Office Career Services Alumni Careers Career Services and Student Resources Career Education and Programming Internships and Fellowships David Bohnett Leadership Fellowship at the L.A. County Board of Supervisors Price Scholars for Community Enrichment Internship Fund International Students Internship Documentation Fall Networking Night Alumni Resources and Programs Employer Resources USC Price Virtual Recruitment and Engagement Fair USC Career Center Employment Data BSPP 2024 Employment Data BSUSP 2024 Employment Data MNLM 2024 Employment Data MHA 2024 Employment Data MPA 2024 Employment Data MPP 2024 Employment Data MUP 2024 Employment Data Contact Us Current Students News All News Events Supporting Price Info Sessions Request Info Apply Menu Open Search University of Southern California Search Site Funding Your Education Undergraduate Scholarships and Financial Aid The following undergraduate scholarships provide partial tuition support to students enrolled in the Price School’s academic degree programs or are USC-affiliated scholarships that are campus-wide. In some cases, receipt of these awards may affect financial aid packages students have already received from USC. Although, in general, additional scholarships may reduce federal work-study and/or federal student loans first, depending on a particular student’s package, these awards may replace gift aid you are receiving from other sources at USC. All scholarships offered through the USC Sol Price School of Public Policy are administered consistent with the University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination. Recipients are chosen without regard to race, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, or any other prohibited characteristic. Subscribe to our scholarship newsletter to be notified of USC and outside scholarship opportunities each month! How to Apply Many scholarships are awarded as part of the admissions process or have deadlines that coincide with admission application deadlines. For this reason, students should begin researching scholarship opportunities early, as many deadlines occur before admission decisions are released. While some scholarships are automatically considered through the admissions process, others require a separate application through Scholarship Universe or directly with the scholarship provider. To maximize your opportunities, complete these three steps: Apply to USC Some scholarships will be granted based on information in your admission application. Merit-based scholarships will be automatically granted to those who qualify and apply by required deadlines. Learn More About Scholarships Apply for Financial Aid Some scholarships may consider your financial need as part of the selection process. Submitting your FAFSA or CADAA will help ensure you can apply to all types of scholarships. Apply for Financial Aid Apply at Scholarship Universe Scholarship Universe is a scholarship matching tool that identifies relevant scholarships based on your personalized profile. Scholarship Universe Undergraduate Scholarships Find Your Scholarships Title Open To Amount Application Opens Deadline How to Apply Disability Advocacy and Leadership Scholarship Details Thanks to the generous support of The Looking Beyond Foundation, scholarship funding has been made available for current USC Price undergraduate students with a demonstrated interest in helping individuals with special needs (physical, mental or emotional disabilities) that interfere with their pursuits and pose as an obstacle. Looking Beyond is a non-profit organization dedicated to promoting awareness and enriching the lives of children and young adults with special needs. Their goal is to impact as many children and young adults with a range of special needs. Incoming students, Continuing students Up to $5,000 December 1, 2026 February 1, 2027 The application is available in Scholarship Universe. Prospective students are automatically considered during the admissions process. Continuing students must apply through Scholarship Universe and login using their USC Net ID and password. Scholarship Universe John and Melinda DiNapoli Endowed Scholarship Details Scholarship for students for whom affordability may be an obstacle. Preference will be given to students earning the Bachelor of Science in Real Estate Development or the Bachelor of Science in Urban Studies and planning who have demonstrated an interest in diversity in these fields. Incoming students, Continuing students Up to $5,000 December 1, 2026 February 1, 2027 The application is available in Scholarship Universe. Prospective students are automatically considered during the admissions process. Continuing students must apply through Scholarship Universe and login using their USC Net ID and password. Scholarship Universe Nick Fagnano Memorial Fund Scholarship Details The Nick Fagnano Memorial Scholarship Fund was established by the Fagnano family in memory of their son Nick Fagnano who passed away just before he was to enter the USC Price School as an undergraduate transfer student. This award is based on academic merit and financial need and will be awarded to a student who reflects Nick’s strength of character. Learn more about Nick and his story here . Continuing students Up to $5,000 December 1, 2026 February 1, 2027 The application is available in Scholarship Universe. Prospective students are automatically considered during the admissions process. Continuing students must apply through Scholarship Universe and login using their USC Net ID and password. Scholarship Universe Perea Family Endowed Scholarship Details Scholarship for Price undergraduates for whom affordability is an obstacle. A positive consideration will be given to students who come from the Central Valley in California and are interested in a public service career that assists Latino communities. Incoming students, Continuing students Up to $5,000 December 1, 2026 February 1, 2027 The application is available in Scholarship Universe. Prospective students are automatically considered during the admissions process. Continuing students must apply through Scholarship Universe and login using their USC Net ID and password. Scholarship Universe Student Undergraduate Research Experience (SURE) Details SURE provides USC Price undergraduates the opportunity to conduct funded research in collaboration with a Price faculty member. Applicants must submit a signed agreement with a Price full-time faculty sponsor, a onepage description of the research plan, and a current STARS report. A detailed budget for how the research funding will be used is also required. The award must only be used to cover costs of the research (may include travel, equipment, living expenses, and other fees associated with the research). Continuing students Up to $2,000 August 1, 2026 May 7, 2027 For questions regarding the application process, please contact: Josephine Le Program Administrator Public Policy: Urban Studies and Planning Phone: (213) 740-2172 Email: [email protected] Email Josephine The Maggie Feiss Scholarship Fund Details The Maggie Feiss Scholarship Fund was established by the family of Maggie Feiss in memory of their daughter and sister, Margaret “Maggie” Oliver Feiss, B.S., Public Policy, Management, and Planning, 2008. Maggie died shortly after graduation, the day before commencing her first post-graduation job. While Maggie had lived with epilepsy from her early teens, she never let it slow her down, and her parents and brother established this scholarship to perpetuate and honor her name, energy and the infectious spirit with which she lived. The Maggie Feiss Scholar shall be a demonstrable risk taker, someone willing to challenge norms in the pursuit of solutions. Continuing students Up to $5,000 December 1, 2026 February 1, 2027 The application is available in Scholarship Universe. Prospective students are automatically considered during the admissions process. Continuing students must apply through Scholarship Universe and login using their USC Net ID and password. Scholarship Universe USC Asian Pacific Alumni Association Scholarships Details The USC Asian Pacific Alumni Association awards scholarships to USC students of exceptional academic merit. Positive consideration may be given in the selection process to students to promote diversity and/or to students who advocate for Asian and Pacific Islander communities. Incoming students, Continuing students Varies Expected December 2026 Expected March 2027 Asian Pacific Alumni Association USC Black Alumni Association Scholarships Details BAA scholarships are based upon the overall profile of a student’s commitment and aspirations gleaned from their application and interview. Scholarships are awarded to USC students on the basis of academic and personal merit in addition to having demonstrated involvement within the African-American community. Incoming students, Continuing students Up to $3,000 Expected December 2026 Expected February 2027 Black Alumni Association USC Lambda LGBTQ+ Association Scholarship Details Since 1994, USC Lambda has awarded over $500,000 in scholarships to more than 150 students who, regardless of their gender or sexual identity, demonstrated academic achievement and a strong commitment to the LGBTQ+ community. These scholars have gone on to executive roles in Fortune 500 companies and LGBTQ+ nonprofits. They have spearheaded research in technology and sociology, produced award-winning films, and argued cases before the United States Supreme Court. They are doctors, educators, artists and activists who inspire our LGBTQ+ student body to see their sexual and gender identities as strengths, not obstacles. Incoming students, Continuing students Varies Expected December 2026 Expected February 2027 Lambda LGBTQ+ Alumni Association USC Latino Alumni Association Scholarships Details LAA provides partial-tuition scholarships to USC undergraduate and graduate students who promote and/or advocate for the Latino/Hispanic community. Graduate scholarships are for master’s candidates only; limited awards for EdD, law, medical, PA, PT, OT, and doctor, of pharmacy students are also available. Incoming students, Continuing students $2,000 to $5,000 for undergraduate students; $500 to $5,000 for graduate students. Expected December 2026 Expected May 2027 Latino Alumni Association USC Norman Topping Student Aid Fund Undergraduate Scholarship Details The Norman Topping Student Aid Fund (NTSAF) assists students with financial need who demonstrate an extraordinary level of community awareness in their pursuit of higher education at the University of Southern California. Applicants residing in areas surrounding the University Park Campus and Health Sciences campus and first-generation college students are given primary consideration in the selection process. Please note that the scholarship is not limited to these populations. Incoming students Up to $5,500 undergraduates December 15, 2026 February 4, 2027 Norman Topping Student Aid Fund USC Town and Gown Scholarships Details Available to U.S. citizens or permanent residents of Southern California with a minimum unweighted GPA of 3.4. Additional considerations include school activities, community engagement, leadership roles and accolades. An interview is required. Incoming students, Continuing students Undergraduates $10,000 per year; Graduate students $15,000 per year July 1, 2026 November 15, 2026 Town and Gown of USC In this section: Request Admission Information Info Sessions & Events Visit USC Price Schedule a Campus Tour Visit Preparation Application Deadlines Funding Your Education Undergraduate Scholarships and Financial Aid Graduate Scholarships and Financial Aid Price Community Enrichment Scholarship Scholarships Spotlight Price Partnerships Talk to a Price Ambassador Mentorship for an Accessible Price (MAP) Meet the MAP Board Price Student Ambassador Program (PSA) On-Campus Master’s Degree Program FAQ Graduate School Fair Schedule Contact USC Price Admission Staff USC Price Ralph and Goldy Lewis Hall 312 Los Angeles, California 90089-0626 (213) 740-0550 Contact Price Donate to Price Stay Informed. Subscribe to The Price Post! Subscribe Media Media Inquiries Price YouTube Newsletters USC Price Blog Podcasts Resources Supporting Price USC Webmail Commencement Current Students Alumni Price Intranet Request Forms Policies Academic Integrity Notice of Non-Discrimination Student Advocacy and Bias Reporting Privacy Policy Accessibility at USC Instagram LinkedIn X TikTok YouTube Facebook Podcasts Flickr Website by Cyberwoven © 2026 University of Southern California	f4201659ca4f2c25eb82ee308dd5a8d122add0ef651f6e16ad751b456cd06165	\N
74	https://sites.usc.edu/new-student-health-requirements/costs/insurance-waiver-requirements/	2026-11-13 18:45:58.153493-08	200	Insurance Waiver Requirements – Health Requirements for Students Skip to content USC Website Toggle search interface Search Search Site Close search interface Menu Toggle extended navigation Health Requirements for Students Start Here Toggle "Start Here" dropdown Read me first! MySHR Quickstart Guide Consent for Treatment Prevention Education Modules Webinars and Resources For Parents Toggle "For Parents" dropdown For Parents (Zhongwen Edition) 致家长（中文版） Required Immunizations Toggle "Required Immunizations" dropdown Uploading Vaccination Records FAQs (Multi-lingual) Signed Vaccine Records (Multi-lingual) Special Clearances: TB Screening (International Students Only) Special Clearances: Clinical Health Professions Special Clearances: DC Cohort Planning Your Care Toggle "Planning Your Care" dropdown Top Tips Students Should Know Medication management or chronic conditions Using Services / Locations Understanding Costs Toggle "Understanding Costs" dropdown Student Health Fee (SHF) Health Insurance Requirement Insurance Waiver Requirements Important Notice: AB 594 Glossary of Health Insurance Terms Contact Toggle "Contact" dropdown Questions? Sign Up for a Chat General FAQs More Menu Toggle extended navigation Insurance Waiver Form Insurance Waiver Rules Home Understanding Costs Insurance Waiver Requirements Insurance Waiver Requirements Your health insurance plan must meet the University’s general waiver requirements outlined below. General Criteria: To satisfy the USC health insurance requirement for students, the plan held by the student must: 1. Be Minimum Essential Coverage ; AND 2. Provide unrestricted access to: An in-network primary care provider, An in-network hospital, and Full, non-emergency medical and behavioral health care These services must be available within a reasonable distance of campus or the student’s residence while attending school. A maximum commuting distance of 50 miles is recommended. Common Reasons for Waiver Denial Your waiver request may be denied if: Your plan provides only emergency or urgent care in your area of study Your plan is a regional HMO or EPO with no network coverage in the Los Angeles area You are enrolled in an out-of-state Medicaid plan (note: these are not accepted for students residing on campus) Your plan is a Healthcare Sharing Program, which is not recognized as insurance and does not guarantee coverage Your plan does not meet the coverage requirements in item 2. Additional Requirements for International Students If you are an international student, please note that most international insurance plans do not meet waiver requirements. Your plan must meet all general waiver criteria above, in addition to meeting U.S. Department of State visa support requirements. Your plan must: Be written in standard English, with all benefits clearly expressed in U.S. dollars Include a claims payment office located in the U.S. (all claims must be processed and paid directly to U.S. providers) Provide a minimum of $50,000 per year for medical evacuation Provide a minimum of $25,000 for repatriation of remains If you have questions regarding your request for a waiver or if you intend to keep the USC Student Health Insurance Plan and have questions, please contact USC Student Health at [email protected] . Keeping SHIP/AETNA Submitting waiver Students who decide to waive SHIP/Aetna must submit a waiver by the third week of classes (Friday). Waivers must be submitted every year in the fall semester by the third Friday deadline. See Fees and Deadlines MySHR Patient Portal 213-740-9355 (WELL) USC Student Health main site CONTACT Location and Hours (213) 740-9355 (WELL) [email protected] Tell Us What You Think SOCIAL Instagram OUR SITES • Sex and Health • Counseling and Mental Health • Confidential Advocates Resources and Education • Staying Well • Athletic Medicine • Insurance 