75	https://sites.usc.edu/new-student-health-requirements/general-faqs/	2026-11-13 18:45:58.153493-08	200	General FAQs – Health Requirements for Students Skip to content USC Website Toggle search interface Search Search Site Close search interface Menu Toggle extended navigation Health Requirements for Students Start Here Toggle "Start Here" dropdown Read me first! MySHR Quickstart Guide Consent for Treatment Prevention Education Modules Webinars and Resources For Parents Toggle "For Parents" dropdown For Parents (Zhongwen Edition) 致家长（中文版） Required Immunizations Toggle "Required Immunizations" dropdown Uploading Vaccination Records FAQs (Multi-lingual) Signed Vaccine Records (Multi-lingual) Special Clearances: TB Screening (International Students Only) Special Clearances: Clinical Health Professions Special Clearances: DC Cohort Planning Your Care Toggle "Planning Your Care" dropdown Top Tips Students Should Know Medication management or chronic conditions Using Services / Locations Understanding Costs Toggle "Understanding Costs" dropdown Student Health Fee (SHF) Health Insurance Requirement Insurance Waiver Requirements Important Notice: AB 594 Glossary of Health Insurance Terms Contact Toggle "Contact" dropdown Questions? Sign Up for a Chat General FAQs More Menu Toggle extended navigation Home General FAQs General FAQs Waivers Can I waive the Student Health Fee (SHF)? No. All students enrolled in 6 or more credits; all international students; and all students enrolled in health professions degree programs are required to pay the student health fee; they then have access to campus health services. This appears on each semester’s student financial account. Can I waive the Student Health Insurance Plan (SHIP)? Yes. If you have a plan that meets the minimum requirements of the university, you may submit documentation to waive the Student Health Insurance Plan (SHIP/Aetna). ONLINE and IN PERSON students who have their own plan must submit a waiver by the Friday of the third week of classes, each fall semester, in order to reverse automatic enrollment in SHIP/Aetna. Immunizations I am in a graduate-level hybrid program (meets online and in person); do I need to meet the immunization requirements? Yes. If you are in an in-person degree program, you are required to meet the immunization requirements. If you think you may have been assaulted while incapacitated/unconscious, we encourage that you still contact an advocate to explore your medical concerns and forensic options as soon as possible after the incident. For more information regarding drug and alcohol facilitated sexual assaults contact an RSVP advocate. I am in a graduate-level online degree program (meets online only); do I need to meet the immunization requirements? No. Only students who are in in-person classes are required to meet the immunization requirements. Copays Are there co-pays for visits to medical or counseling appointments in Student Health? No. There are no co-pays or other out-of-pocket visit fees, or billing to insurance, for appointment visits with providers in Student Health. Insurance does apply for lab and radiology services, immunizations, and care-related equipment (crutches and boots). Note: Provider services outside of Student Health (for example, Psychiatry and Behavioral Health Services, the private practice on the 5th floor of Engemann), prescriptions and pharmacy services, etc., may require co-pays when using your insurance. Patient Privacy Are my records kept confidential ? Yes. Your records are private and confidential in compliance with ethical and legal standards including FERPA and HIPAA. Immunizations/Insurance Deadline is Jan 29, 2027 Complete your immunizations by the first day of classes (January 11, 2027). If you cannot complete requirements before coming to campus, you are required to come to the immunizations fair (“Immu-Fair”) during the first week of classes. If your immunization records are incomplete by Jan 29, 2027 , a registration hold will be applied to your student account. Review and make a decision on health insurance by this same deadline date. If you choose to use your own insurance (must meet minimum criteria) and waive the SHIP/Aetna plan, you must do so by this date, or the SHIP/Aetna plan and the relevant premiums will be non-reversible on your student account. Immunization Documentation Examples Please note that records must show your name and date of birth in order to be accepted. Screenshots for health portal records are accepted. For records in languages other than English, translations into English must be provided. Example of a PRC immunization card/booklet Translated Immunizations Example of a lab report Please note that lab reports should include the following information to verify: a. Patient’s Full Name b. Patient’s Date of Birth c. Name of Test Performed d. Date of Test e. Test Result Numeric Values (cannot just say “positive” or “negative”) f. Test Reference Ranges g. Ordering Provider Name CONTACT Location and Hours (213) 740-9355 (WELL) [email protected] Tell Us What You Think SOCIAL Instagram OUR SITES • Sex and Health • Counseling and Mental Health • Confidential Advocates Resources and Education • Staying Well • Athletic Medicine • Insurance (SHIP) ABOUT US Mission, Values, and Vision Annual Report 2025-2026 LEADERS & PROVIDERS Leadership Meet the Providers JOIN OUR TEAM Employment Opportunities Training for College Mental Health Professionals Student Jobs INTRANET Intranet (Log-in required) POLICIES / INFORMATION Patient Privacy and Confidentiality Patient Rights and Responsibilities Medical Policies and Forms FEES Fees and Deadlines List For Online Degree Program Students INTERPRETER SERVICES Available upon request UPDATES Staying Well at USC Patient Materials HEALTHY CAMPUS AND WELLBEING PARTNERS Newsletter Wellbeing Collective ONE Safety USC Guides for Faculty Student Health Advisory Committee Meet the Health Promotion Strategy Team University of Southern California Privacy Notice Notice of Non-Discrimination Digital Accessibility close menu Search Search Site Start Here Toggle "Start Here" submenu Read me first! MySHR Quickstart Guide Consent for Treatment Prevention Education Modules Webinars and Resources For Parents Required Immunizations Toggle "Required Immunizations" submenu Uploading Vaccination Records FAQs (Multi-lingual) Signed Vaccine Records (Multi-lingual) Special Clearances: TB Screening (International Students Only) Special Clearances: Clinical Health Professions Special Clearances: DC Cohort Planning Your Care Toggle "Planning Your Care" submenu Top Tips Students Should Know Medication management or chronic conditions Using Services / Locations Understanding Costs Toggle "Understanding Costs" submenu Student Health Fee (SHF) Health Insurance Requirement Insurance Waiver Requirements Important Notice: AB 594 Glossary of Health Insurance Terms Contact Toggle "Contact" submenu Questions? Sign Up for a Chat General FAQs	134e354dd91dcfa046e937d08068cd871fe56b1ed2acd6782cd6bb185027db86	\N
