48	https://campussupport.usc.edu/	2026-11-13 18:45:58.153493-08	200	Campus Support and Intervention - Campus Support & Intervention Skip to main content Go to usc.edu homepage Campus Support & Intervention Home About Us Students Show submenu for Students First-Time Consultation Academics Health & Wellness Show submenu for Health & Wellness Health Leave Basic Needs Crisis & Safety Emergency Loan Application Faculty & Staff Show submenu for Faculty & Staff Report a Concern Resources Families, Parents & Guardians TC4T Health Leave Show submenu for Health Leave Resources & Forms Frequently Asked Questions More… Show More Menu Search for: Campus Support and Intervention Support for USC The Office of Campus Support & Intervention (CSI) is where members of the Trojan community go to seek support for themselves, for others, and for the community. We are a one-stop shop for care and support, troubleshooting, and advocacy. If you would like to connect with a CSI team member, please call at 213-740-0411 or email at uscsupport@usc.edu . A member of our team will respond to emails within one business day. Health Leave of Absence for Students For more information about the Health Leave process, including how to schedule an online appointment, please visit our Health Leave page. Who We Are Campus Support & Intervention (CSI) is an office within Campus Wellbeing and Crisis Intervention. Our team is here to assist current students, faculty, and staff in navigating complex issues. Whether you are here seeking support for yourself or someone else, we are available to help you problem solve, understand options, and connect with resources. Please note that we are not an emergency resource and are not available 24/7. In case of an emergency, please contact the Department of Public Safety at 213-740-4321. What We Do Students, faculty, and staff may encounter challenges that disrupt their ability to succeed and meet their goals. CSI is dedicated to helping individuals get back on track by providing options and pathways for success. We connect with members of the USC community when they need support in achieving their academic, professional, or personal goals. Our consultations, available in person, via Zoom, or over the phone, allow us to understand each individual’s situation so we can offer troubleshooting, support, guidance, and connections to relevant campus and community resources. Below are some of the ways CSI serves the USC community: Navigation of complex issues and challenges Resource referrals and recommendations Critical incident response and postvention support Solutions and options Trojans Care 4 Trojans (TC4T) – A reporting program for concerns about someone’s well-being Professor notifications* DPS incident follow-up Student Health Leave of Absence Crisis as you define it *Notifications are made on a case-by-case basis when a student is unable to make the notifications on their own behalf. Please consult with a staff member regarding these requests. Students Need support, but don’t know where to start? Discover the resources available to you and schedule to speak directly with a team member. Faculty & Staff Are you a faculty or staff member seeking support? Explore the resources available to you. If you’re concerned about a student, CSI can collaborate with you to provide outreach and assistance. Families, Parents & Guardians Worried about your student? Learn about some of the resources available to them and how you can partner with CSI to support them through any challenges they may be facing. Trojans Care 4 Trojans (TC4T) USC Trojans Care for Trojans (TC4T) is an initiative within the Office of Campus Wellbeing and Crisis Intervention that empowers USC students, faculty and staff to take action when they are concerned about a fellow Trojan challenged with personal difficulties. This private and anonymous request form provides an opportunity for Trojans to help a member of our Trojan Family. Submit a concern Campus Support & Intervention Tutor Campus Center, TCC Suite 421 Los Angeles, CA 90089 (213) 740-0411 uscsupport@usc.edu Related Sites Campus Wellbeing & Crisis Intervention Campus Wellbeing & Education USC Office of the Ombuds Concerned about a USC community member? TC4T is a private and anonymous form to help a member of the Trojan Family. Submit a concern University Links University Human Resources Office for Equity, Equal Opportunity, and Title IX Office of Professionalism and Ethics Office of Culture, Ethics, and Compliance How to Report a Concern – USC Report & Response University of Southern California Built using the USC Gateway 2018 WordPress Theme | Website issues? Contact USC Provost IT Privacy Notice | Notice of Non-discrimination | Digital Accessibility | Sitemap Translate	602938ded5dbd33888140797112ae034228d92d208316211c095e6ccee9d8c95	\N
49	https://campussupport.usc.edu/students/basic-needs/emergency-loan-application/	2026-11-13 18:45:58.153493-08	200	Emergency Loan Application - Campus Support & Intervention Skip to main content Go to usc.edu homepage Campus Support & Intervention Home About Us Students Show submenu for Students First-Time Consultation Academics Health & Wellness Show submenu for Health & Wellness Health Leave Basic Needs Crisis & Safety Emergency Loan Application Faculty & Staff Show submenu for Faculty & Staff Report a Concern Resources Families, Parents & Guardians TC4T Health Leave Show submenu for Health Leave Resources & Forms Frequently Asked Questions More… Show More Menu Search for: Emergency Loan Application For students struggling with severe financial hardship *UPDATE: Emergency Loan Applications – Fall 2026 The Emergency Loan Application is currently closed for the Fall 2026 semester. Students seeking additional support are encouraged to review available resources or contact our office with questions about other resources that may be appropriate. The Campus Support & Intervention (CSI) Emergency Loan program is available for students who have experienced an unforeseen financial emergency. Students may receive one loan per/semester not exceeding $1,000. Students are highly encouraged to consult with the Financial Aid Office and their respective academic unit prior to applying for an emergency loan. Eligibility Currently enrolled Good financial standing with USC – does not have a negative balance in collections U.S.A. issued Social Security Number Must demonstrate need by providing documentation verifying the emergency Must demonstrate the financial capacity to fulfill repayment obligations What is an Emergency? Family emergency, loss of employment, natural disasters, medical emergencies and other unexpected issues that suddenly change your financial circumstances Policy Details CSI may approve loans of up to $1000 per student. Please allow five to ten business days for processing. Emergency loans must be repaid through Student Financial Services within 90 days. If an emergency loan is not repaid within 90 days, a 10% annual interest rate will be applied, the account will be sent to collections, and a registration hold will be placed. Failure to repay will also result in students becoming ineligible for future emergency loans. CSI reserves the right to decline any application, regardless of eligibility. Emergency Loan Application Form Please fill out the form below and someone from Campus Support & Intervention will contact you within one to two business days. Full Name (Required) First Last Student ID (Required) Do you have a Social Security Number? (Required) A SSN is required for the loan application. Upon approval, a staff member will contact you via phone to obtain it. Yes No Current Address (Required) Street Address City Alabama Alaska American Samoa Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Guam Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Northern Mariana Islands Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Puerto Rico Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah U.S. Virgin Islands Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Armed Forces Americas Armed Forces Europe Armed Forces Pacific State ZIP Code Cell Phone (Required) Email Address Are you currently enrolled as a student at USC? Yes No Are you currently employed in a paying position? Yes No Are you currently receiving financial aid? Yes No Describe your efforts to obtain assistance through other sources. (Financial Aid appeal, academic unit, family, friends, organizations, etc.) Describe how you will be able to repay the emergency loan within 90 days. Describe your financial situation in your own words. Include what expenses the emergency fund would be used for and attach appropriate documentation to this application. Please share with us anything you feel is relevant. Please upload supporting documentation explaining your financial situation. While it is not required in order to submit your Emergency Loan application, supporting documentation will allow us to review your request more quickly and accurately. If you choose not to include supporting documentation, it might be requested after your application is submitted, which could delay the review process further. Drop files here or Select files Max. file size: 15 MB. Emergency loan amount you are requesting Please enter a number less than or equal to 1000 . CAPTCHA Email This field is for validation purposes and should be left unchanged. Campus Support & Intervention Tutor Campus Center, TCC Suite 421 Los Angeles, CA 90089 (213) 740-0411 uscsupport@usc.edu Related Sites Campus Wellbeing & Crisis Intervention Campus Wellbeing & Education USC Office of the Ombuds Concerned about a USC community member? TC4T is a private and anonymous form to help a member of the Trojan Family. Submit a concern University Links University Human Resources Office for Equity, Equal Opportunity, and Title IX Office of Professionalism and Ethics Office of Culture, Ethics, and Compliance How to Report a Concern – USC Report & Response University of Southern California Built using the USC Gateway 2018 WordPress Theme | Website issues? Contact USC Provost IT Privacy Notice | Notice of Non-discrimination | Digital Accessibility | Sitemap Translate	e45c99de830e7044d81ad2f76c2a6a356c6dcae0d9c1acde0a690b502fc9bae3	\N
50	https://careers.usc.edu/channels/appointments/	2026-11-13 18:45:58.153493-08	200	Appointments – Career Center | University of Southern California Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Career Center Schedule An Appointment Handshake Who We Serve Audiences Incoming Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Ph.D.’s & Postdoctoral Students Employers Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Affinities First-Generation Students International Students Student Accessibility Veteran Students Our Services Appointments Workshops & Trojan Talks Career Fairs & Events Professional Headshots Scholarships Trojan Network Make A Request Online Resources Get Career Ready Career Exploration Career Readiness Competencies Explore Industries Resumes/Cover Letters/Curriculum Vitaes Mentors & Networking Interview Preparation Offer Negotiation Financial Literacy Education and Events AI Guidelines Find Internships & Jobs On-Campus Jobs Campus Recruiting Handshake Internship Guide Job Search Guide Trojan Network Trojan Accountability Expectations Connect With Us About Us Get Involved Meet the Team Meet Our Partners School-Based Career Services Report a Fraudulent Job Posting Career Outcomes First Destination Survey Summer Experience Survey Appointments Find information on making appointments and requests below. 24/7 Support Looking for Resume Assistance NOW? Career Center Resume Guide Quinncia is USC’s new AI career prep platform available to current students starting Fall 2026 Generative AI Guidelines for resume prompts when using Generative AI Want Interviewing Support NOW? The USC Career Center is proud to provide all students and alumni with Big Interview – an interactive platform that provides 24/7 access to interview practice opportunities, customized feedback, etc. Current students can also access Quinncia for additional mock interviewing prep based on your resume upload. Interested in a career assessment NOW? The Your Next Step platform provides various career assessments and helps clarify career goals. This resource offers you access to career opportunities, prepares you for interviews, and assists you in executing a strategic job search. Interested in specialized resources? Many school-based career centers have curated resources and services specifically for the students in their majors. Please consider making an appointment with a career advisor from your school-based career center. Drop-in Advising Drop-in advising is designed to help students connect with a career advisor to ask basic career questions, explore career resources, or get a quick critique of your resume or cover letter. Fall & Spring: Drop-in advising is available in-person in STU 110 from 1:00-3:30 pm Summer: 15-minute resume review critiques are available via appointment on Handshake Many school-based career centers provide school-specific advising as well. For resume and cover letter support, we encourage you to use the following resources: Resume Resources on Handshake to view the USC Career Center online resource library on Handshake Cover Letter, Resume, and CV guide with samples to review Resume workshops featured on the USC Career Center YouTube channel Details: Each drop-in session is 10-15 minutes. Drop-ins are available on a first-come, first-served basis. During peak times, students may be asked to participate in group drop-in advising sessions to ensure timely support for everyone. An active Handshake account is required to check-in for all drop-ins. Log in to Handshake and complete your student profile to activate your account. Students are limited to one advising contact per day (appointment or drop-in advising). Scheduled Appointments Career Advisors provide 30-minute appointments via phone, Zoom or in-person. Many school-based career centers have career advisors to schedule appointments with as well. During scheduled 30-minute appointments, USC Career Center advisors typically advise on the following topics: Career Development Internship and Job Search Informational Interviews & Networking Offer/Salary Negotiation Mock Interviews Note: If you want the Career Advisors to tailor interview questions for you, please email the advisor you are scheduled with and provide your resume and a copy of a job description at least two business days in advance after your appointment request is confirmed. Please note: Resume critiques are only conducted during drop-in advising (1:00 pm – 3:30 pm Monday through Friday, no appointment needed) To schedule a 30-minute appointment: Log in to Handshake . Go to Career Center, then click on Appointments. Click “ Schedule a New Appointment ” and choose USC Career Center – Current Students. Search for available appointments that meet your needs. You will have the opportunity to select either a virtual or in-person appointment. If you opt for a virtual session please be specific in the appointment request notes and be sure to indicate whether you prefer to have your appointment via phone or video chat (Zoom). Video appointment: the advisor will email you a Zoom link to your USC email address once the appointment is approved. Learn how to create your Zoom account . Phone appointment: please include your phone number in your appointment request. In-person appointments: Will be held in USC Career Center lobby (Student Union, Suite 110, University Park Campus). Undergraduate Students Our policy is one appointment (drop-in or 30-minute) per day, so please plan accordingly. Graduate Students Are limited to one advising appointment with the central Career Center before being referred to your college for more industry-specific advising. Graduate students are encouraged to attend Career Center workshops, fairs, and other events and utilize online resources available in Handshake. Non-degree Students Please be advised that career advising appointments and drop-ins are for current students in certificate and degree programs. Pre-master’s students may request appointments upon enrollment in Master’s coursework. If you have any questions please email careers@usc.edu Students Responsibility in Scheduling Career Appointments Once your scheduled career advising appointment is approved, please ensure you attend your meeting or cancel within 48 hours or two business days prior to your appointment. If you need to cancel your career advising appointment, please email careers@usc.edu or call 213 740-9111 and leave a message. If you fail to cancel within 48 hours, your career advising privileges may be revoked. Alumni (0-3 years following graduation) Please refer to the Alumni Career page for advising information. Additional questions can be directed to careers@usc.edu Mock Interview Appointments Scheduled a mock interview? If you want us to tailor mock interview questions, please email your career advisor at least two full business days before your appointment with: A detailed job description of interest A recent copy of your resume Please review Interview Preparation for additional tips. If you do not send us a job description, the advisor will ask you general interview questions. We highly encourage you to practice interviewing BEFORE your mock interview using Big Interview or Quinncia . This 24/7 resource allows you to select interview questions, record and review your answers. Online Resources The USC Career Center offers multiple resources to help individuals explore their career opportunities. We have curated several of our favorite resources to help discover career paths, learn about internship positions, and find full-time jobs. Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link Handshake Updated June 19, 2026 Handshake is USC’s university-wide career services management platform and the largest career community for college students. … Read More School-Based Career Services Share This: Share School-Based Career Services on Facebook Share School-Based Career Services on 