70	https://itservices.usc.edu/usc-computing-center-laptop-loaner-program/	2026-11-13 18:45:58.153493-08	200	USC Computing Center Laptop Loaner Program – USC Information Technology Services Skip to content USC Website Toggle search interface Search Search Site Close search interface Menu Toggle extended navigation USC Information Technology Services Home Log Me In Toggle "Log Me In" dropdown Activate your USC NetID Account AdaptiveWork Brightspace LMS ChatGPT Edu (AI) Docusign Gemini Notebook (AI) Gmail for Faculty Google Gemini (AI) ITS Service Portal (ServiceNow) Microsoft Copilot Chat (AI) Office 365 Qualtrics Workday Zoom Get Help Toggle "Get Help" dropdown Change My Password Self Help: Find Answers in Knowledge Articles Report an Issue Check on my ticket: ITS Service Portal Contact the Customer Support Center Report a Security Issue Find Services Toggle "Find Services" dropdown Find Services – Service Portal Browse Services – A to Z Strategic Initiatives Toggle "Strategic Initiatives" dropdown Enterprise Artificial Intelligence (AI) Services For Students – Find Services For Faculty & Researchers – Find Services For IT Professionals – Find Services For Staff – Find Services For Visitors – Find Services About ITS Toggle "About ITS" dropdown Contact Us Information Security ITS Strategic Priorities Leadership Local IT Support Directory News Resources & Links Toggle "Resources & Links" dropdown Center for Advanced Research Computing (CARC.usc.edu) ITS Service Portal (ServiceNow) Learning Environments LosNettos.net Room Finder Software.usc.edu TrojanSecure.usc.edu USC Online Status Dashboard AI at USC Toggle "AI at USC" dropdown AI Software Available at USC Toggle "AI Software Available at USC" dropdown Login to ChatGPT Login to Microsoft Copilot Chat Login to Google Gemini Login to Gemini Notebook ITS Alerts More Menu Toggle extended navigation Home USC Computing Center Laptop Loaner Program USC Computing Center Laptop Loaner Program Features Laptops are updated with the most recent operating system Laptops are equipped with the same software packages available on computing center desktops. Laptops can connect to the USC Guest Wireless and USC Secure Wireless networks, allowing you to work outside the computing center environment. Laptops may be checked out for four hours. You will be emailed confirmation of the laptop loan and the required time of return. Late fees will be assessed for the late return of any laptop. See Pricing below for more information. Confirmation of the loan renewal and required time of return will be emailed. Eligibility This service is only available to currently enrolled USC students with a valid USC Card. Students may be excluded from the laptop loan service at ITS’s discretion for repeated late laptop returns, damage, or loss of loaned laptops. Rentals are available for up to 4 hours and can be extended for an additional 4 hours. Laptop rentals are available in the basement of Leavy Library. To reserve a laptop, please visit the ITS Desk. You must present a valid USC card to be scanned and fill out the Student Laptop Loan Agreement . Pricing First four-hour loan: No charge Four-hour renewal, if arranged prior to the expiration of first four-hour loan: No charge Late return of loaned laptop: $20.00 for every 30 minutes late, up to the replacement cost of the laptop. Email reminders for late returns and late fees assessed are sent to the student. NOTE: Computing accessories may also be checked out by faculty, staff, and students at the USC Computing Centers. Available accessories include: HDMI adapters Computer mice Learning Environments Support Call the ITS Learning Environments team at (213) 821-6601 or email spaces@usc.edu . Submit a Classroom Equipment Request on the ITS Service Portal . Customized instruction on the use of specific equipment or a specific classroom is available for your convenience and individual needs by submitting a Request for Technology Orientation on the ITS Service Portal . Request classroom technology training on the ITS Service Portal . Request learning space and audiovisual systems design, consulting, and project management services on the ITS Service Portal . Reserve a Classroom through the Office of Academic Records and Registrar Office . Student Laptop Loan Agreement I agree that I am responsible for returning this laptop on time in the same condition as when I borrowed it. I understand that: If, after an ITS staff inspection, it is determined that I damaged the laptop screen, hardware, and/or casing, I will be charged repair or replacement costs. If, after an ITS staff inspection, it is determined that I did not return all cables or accessories, I will be charged replacement costs. If I tamper with the equipment, I will be charged to repair or replace the laptop and any cables or accessories and may also be subject to disciplinary action. If I fail to return the laptop on time to the same location from which I borrowed it, I will be fined $20 for the first 30 minutes and $20 for each successive 30 minutes after the due time, up to the total cost of a replacement laptop. ITS is not responsible for damage to data caused by viruses that may exist on the network or are spread through the network or from software malfunctions. ITS is not responsible for damage to external drives or any other devices plugged into the laptop. I cannot save files on the laptop’s hard drive and must save my files by copying them to another location (for example a USB flash drive). All files left on the laptop will be erased. ITS accepts no responsibility for lost files. I agree to abide by USC’s Computing Policies: https://www.usc.edu/its/policies . I understand that by borrowing this laptop, I am responsible for its return. I agree never to leave the laptop unattended or in someone else’s care. If the laptop is stolen while on loan to me, I am responsible for the entire replacement cost of the equipment. ITS Support The ITS Service Desk provides support to the USC community 24 hours a day, 365 days a year. Call (213) 740-5555 and choose option 2 to receive assistance. Please note that some requests may require a government ID for user verification. Report an Issue on the ITS Service Portal . Search for information on the ITS Service Portal . FIND SERVICES Browse Services For Students For Faculty and Researchers For Staff For Visitors GET HELP Contact Us ITS Alerts Find Answers Report an Issue ITS Service Portal ABOUT ITS Local IT Support Information Security News Leadership Give Feedback CUSTOMER SUPPORT CENTER 213-740-5555 (24x7) Contact Us Report a Security Issue For any requests to change content, contact ITS Communications . University of Southern California Privacy Notice Notice of Non-Discrimination Digital Accessibility close menu Search Search Site Home Log Me In Toggle "Log Me In" submenu Activate your USC NetID Account AdaptiveWork Brightspace LMS ChatGPT Edu (AI) Docusign Gemini Notebook (AI) Gmail for Faculty Google Gemini (AI) ITS Service Portal (ServiceNow) Microsoft Copilot Chat (AI) Office 365 Qualtrics Workday Zoom Get Help Toggle "Get Help" submenu Change My Password Self Help: Find Answers in Knowledge Articles Report an Issue Check on my ticket: ITS Service Portal Contact the Customer Support Center Report a Security Issue Find Services Toggle "Find Services" submenu Find Services – Service Portal Browse Services – A to Z Strategic Initiatives For Students – Find Services For Faculty & Researchers – Find Services For IT Professionals – Find Services For Staff – Find Services For Visitors – Find Services About ITS Toggle "About ITS" submenu Contact Us Information Security ITS Strategic Priorities Leadership Local IT Support Directory News Resources & Links Toggle "Resources & Links" submenu Center for Advanced Research Computing (CARC.usc.edu) ITS Service Portal (ServiceNow) Learning Environments LosNettos.net Room Finder Software.usc.edu TrojanSecure.usc.edu USC Online Status Dashboard AI at US