romise) so the app never overstates a benefit for grad students.\nFIELD: one optional profile field, "financial aid status" (sensitive). Asked only when it would unlock this match, with a "why we ask" line, never inferred, deletable. Until answered, the result is "maybe", with the question: "Do you receive financial aid at USC?"\nSplit from candidate 25 (graduate rule), owner decision 2026-11-13.	{provider}	candidates_batch2.md #25	## 25. financial-aid-appeal: Financial aid special circumstances appeal  [DECISION MADE BY ASSISTANT, owner to confirm]\n- category: cash | relevance: money\n- how to apply: submit the appeal and supporting documents through the "Required Info and Forms" page of your FAST portal; each appeal is reviewed once and decisions are final; submit at least 30 days before the end of the term. Examples that may qualify: significant involuntary loss of income, death of a parent or spouse, divorce after the FAFSA, extraordinary out-of-pocket medical costs, budget increases for things like childcare, books, rent above the standard budget.\n- two rules, stored separately:\n  - UNDERGRADUATE rule: eligibility = level undergraduate AND receives or applied for financial aid AND has a change in circumstances. Benefit label: "If approved, you may receive supplemental grant funding; it may not cover the full need." value null.\n  - GRADUATE rule: eligibility = level graduate AND receives or applied for financial aid AND has a change in circumstances. Benefit label: "A re-evaluation of your budget. For graduate students a budget increase is usually funded with loans, not grants." value null.\n- DECISION: the pages disagree on grants for grad students. The grad appeals page lists budget increases funded with PLUS loans or private financing, and the grad "Next Steps" page says re-evaluations will not result in grants or increased loan amounts. I store the cautious version above (loans, no grant promise) so the app never overstates a benefit for grad students.\n- FIELD: one optional profile field, "financial aid status" (sensitive). Asked only when it would unlock this match, with a "why we ask" line, never inferred, deletable. Until answered, the result is "maybe", with the question: "Do you receive financial aid at USC?"\n- sources: https://financialaid.usc.edu/undergraduate-financial-aid/admitted-and-continuing-students/special-circumstances-and-appeals-undergaduate-continuing/ and https://financialaid.usc.edu/graduate-professional-financial-aid/admitted-and-continuing-students/special-circumstances-and-appeals/\n- key quote: "you can submit an appeal through your FAST portal"\n	manoj	2026-11-13 11:50:28.304335-08	25	2026-11-13 11:37:37.427104-08	2026-11-13 12:24:20.155975-08	[]
